Zhang Guangjun was appointed deputy governor of Guangdong Province.
The fifth meeting of the Standing Committee of the 13th National People's Congress of Guangdong Province held its second plenary meeting in Guangzhou on the 30th.
After voting, the meeting decided to appoint Zhang Guangjun as the deputy governor of the People's Government of Guangdong Province.
Previously, Zhang Guangjun was the deputy secretary of the party committee of the China Engineering Physics Research Institute.
Comrade Zhang Guangjun's resume: Zhang Guangjun, male, Han Chinese, born in February 1968, Chongqing, joined the party in April 1994, participated in the work in July 1991, graduated from the Department of Radio Engineering of Harbin University of Technology in electronic instruments and measurement technology, university degree, senior engineer, enjoy the special allowance experts of the State Council government.
He is currently the deputy governor of the Guangdong provincial government and a member of the party group.
From 1987 to 1991, he studied electronic instruments and measurement technology in the Department of Radio Engineering of Harbin University of Technology.
1991-1998 Technical staff of the Institute of General Engineering of the Chinese Academy of Engineering Physics, deputy director of the department, secretary and deputy director of the party branch
From 1998 to 2002, deputy director of the General Engineering Research Institute of the China Academy of Engineering Physics and deputy secretary of the party committee (of which: 1999.05-2000.12 also served as the secretary of the Disciplinary Committee of the Research Institute, 2001.09-2001.12).
2002-2002 Party Secretary and Deputy Director of the General Engineering Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Engineering Physics (during which: 2002.03-2004.05 Fudan University School of Management, Graduate Course in Management Science and Engineering)
2002-2009 Director of the Political Department of the Chinese Academy of Engineering Physics, Director of the Office of the Party Committee and Vice-President of the Party School (during which: 2005.09-2006.01 Young cadre training course)
From 2009 to 2014, the director of the Office of Major Special Management of the China Academy of Engineering Physics (during which: 2011.09-2012.01 Young cadre training courses in the Central Party School)
2014-2015 Assistant Dean of the China Academy of Engineering Physics and Director of the Office of Major Engineering Management
Deputy Secretary of the Party Committee of the China Academy of Engineering Physics 2015-2018
In September 2018, he was the deputy governor of the Guangdong provincial government and a member of the party group.
According to British media, Admiral William Moran, Undersecretary for U.S. Naval Operations, said that even as the U.S. Navy is reviving its forces to deal with an increasingly worrisome Russia on both sides of the Atlantic, the U.S. will continue to focus its navies in the Asia-Pacific region, which the Pentagon has expanded to include the Indo-Asia-Pacific.
According to the British "Jane's Defense Weekly" website reported on September 24, the United States announced at the beginning of the new national defense strategy to China and Russia as a strategic competitor.
Since then, the U.S. Navy has restored the Second Fleet in order to confront Russian activities more directly.
The moves have raised questions and concerns among allies and analysts that the U.S. Navy could stay away from the “Asia-Pacific rebalancing” strategy that marks the Obama administration.
But General Moran said the U.S. Navy’s focus is still on the Western Pacific.
“There have been no significant changes for us,” he said at a round-table discussion titled “Responding to the Challenges of the High Seas,” hosted by the U.S. Bureau of Asian Studies in Washington on January 24, 2018.
â€œThe focus is still on rebalancing, shifting the center of gravity, or no matter how youâ€TMs trying to describe it,â€ Moran said.
However, he admitted that the United States is closely related to Europe.
“We’re going to keep an eye on growth on the West Coast and balance what we can do,” he said.
While Moran noted that overall policy on Russia falls within the purview of the U.S. Secretary of Defense, he warned: “Russians may face demographic and economic challenges, but history proves that if we clash with them, they’re going to be very tough.”
As part of the U.S. resurgent operation against Russia, China, and other contenders, the U.S. Navy is dynamically deploying troops into a "new mode of operation," General Moran said, which will help put adversaries off swiff in the deployment of U.S. aircraft carrier battle groups or other assets at any given time and place.
“Our Navy and Marine Corps support it—the concept of operational unpredictability, don’t be in the same place again and again, almost like clockwork — and that’s what we’re doing,” he said.
One of the first to try this new approach was the Harry S. Truman carrier strike group, whose early deployments included working visits to the port and patrols in areas that normally only passed.
Moran said the U.S. Navy is currently working to ensure that allies are aware that these ships will still patrol traditional areas and are also addressing logistical and family liaison issues for new deployment procedures.
Lt. Gen. Michael Noonan, commander of the Royal Australian Navy, also spoke at the event, saying that the Australian military can work seamlessly with the U.S. carrier strike group.
He said that this will continue as the Royal Australian Navy plans to purchase nine more frigates equipped with Aegis combat systems.
From October 5, a number of airlines will raise or restore fuel surcharges, and there will be more money for aircraft travel from next Friday.
Yesterday, Xiangpeng Airlines, Aokai Airlines and other airlines announced that from October 5, 2018 (ticketing date), the domestic route fuel surcharge below 800 km (inclusive) per passenger charged 20 yuan fuel surcharge, more than 800 kilometers per passenger charged 30 yuan fuel surcharge.
Xiangpeng Airlines, Aokai Airlines and other companies announced that since October 5, 2018, from 0:00 on October 5, 2018, the fuel surcharge charging standard for domestic routes below 800 kilometers (inclusive) has increased from 10 yuan / person to 20 yuan / person, and the fuel surcharge on domestic routes above 800 kilometers has been increased from 10 yuan per passenger to 30 yuan / person.
Children, military and police disability are 10 yuan / person; the baby continues to be exempted.
According to the relevant person in charge of Ctrip's ticket, it has been noted in the notice that the fuel surcharge is charged on the original issue date, and when the ticket is exchanged, the fuel surcharge is not refunded.
This means that the domestic route ticket issued before October 5, if it is to be changed to October 5 (inclusive), it is not necessary to pay fuel surcharges according to the new standard.
Since June 5, 2018, many airlines such as Air China, China Eastern Airlines, HNA, Shanghai Airlines, Spring and Autumn Airlines, Shenzhen Airlines, Western Airlines, Okai Airlines and many other airlines have resumed collecting fuel surcharges on domestic routes that have been cancelled for three years, charging a standard of 10 yuan / person.
This time, Xiangpeng Airlines and Aokai Airlines took the lead in announcing the increase in fuel surcharges, and as of the press release, they have not yet seen the news that four major domestic airlines have announced follow-up adjustments.
It is also understood that the Civil Aviation Department of Hong Kong stipulates that airlines can decide whether to collect fuel surcharges from November.
Cathay Pacific announced as early as September 27 that it will pay fuel surcharges from November 2.
According to Cathay Pacific's website, all Cathay Pacific and Cathay Dragon tickets issued or reissued on or after 2 November will include a fuel surcharge for long-distance flights between Hong Kong and the South-West Pacific, North America, Europe, the Middle East and India regions and Africa, with a fuel surcharge of $652 and a fee of $146 for short-haul flights.
Fees apply to all types of tickets, are calculated for each segment, and are included in the ticket quotations for all direct sales channels in Cathay Pacific.
On the eve of the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang met with the new diplomatic envoys of 29 countries and regions in the Great Hall of the People on the afternoon of the 30th
Li Keqiang shook hands and cordially with the envoys in China one by one.
Li Keqiang welcomed the envoys to China and asked them to convey sincere greetings and good wishes to the leaders of all relevant countries, the people and leaders of relevant institutions.
Li Keqiang commented positively on China's good relations with other countries and regions, stressing that China is committed to enhancing bilateral political mutual trust, deepening practical cooperation, strengthening coordination and cooperation in international and regional affairs, and hopes that the envoys will walk more and look more and make new positive contributions to promoting the development of China's relations with their respective countries and regions in their new positions.
The Chinese Government is willing to facilitate and support envoys in the performance of their duties.
Li Keqiang pointed out that China adheres to the path of peaceful development and unswervingly promotes economic globalization.
This year marks the 40th anniversary of China's reform and opening up, and as the world's largest developing country, we are willing to achieve common development with other countries in further opening up.
In the context of rising protectionism and unilateralism, we are willing to work with all parties to continue to consolidate and strengthen partnerships based on the principles of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit, promote docking and development strategies, promote the construction and cooperation of the "Belt and Road" in accordance with the principle of joint consultation, joint construction and sharing, work together to safeguard multilateralism and free trade, jointly build an open world economy, and inject new impetus into promoting the stable and balanced development of the world economy.
The envoys of various countries and institutions in China warmly congratulated the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China, conveyed the greetings of the leaders of their respective countries and institutions to the leaders of China's leaders, and said that China's development achievements are outstanding, and believe that further deepening reforms and expanding opening up in the future will bring more development opportunities to the world.
It is willing to play a positive role in promoting friendly cooperation between their respective countries and regions with China and better achieving mutual benefit and win-win results.
Subsequently, diplomatic envoys from various countries and institutions in China attended Li Keqiang's National Day reception at the invitation.
State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the event.
Japan's Ito-Tchş Corporation on Friday identified $1.3 billion in impairment losses on China's CITIC shares as a result of a write-down on its largest corporate investment deal due to trade tensions between China and the United States.
In May 2016, in Tokyo, Japan, a man walked past the headquarters of Maru Red Co., Ltd.
Maru Hong said that Gao Hong, its U.S. grain division, has suspended financial transactions in agriculture.
Some of Japan's heavy equipment manufacturers, telecommunications companies, etc. have warned about the impact of Sino-US trade frictions when they announced their latest results, and now these Japanese trading agencies have joined the ranks.
The U.S. and the U.S. impose tariffs on each other’s hundreds of billions of dollars of goods, and U.S. President Donald Trump has threatened to extend the tax to more than $500 billion of Chinese goods if the dispute cannot be resolved.
Tsuyoshi Hachimura, chief commercial finance officer of Itochong, said next year's trade dispute could have a greater impact on China's economy.
Itochu Corporation and Thailand’s Bee Group invested $10 billion in CITIC in 2015 and acquired a 20 percent stake.
Hachimura said that Ito Ctātła Corporation lost 143.3 billion yen ($1.3 billion) on this part of its holdings, due to the belief that CITIC's stock price will not pick up in the near future.
Itochu Corporation maintained its profit forecast for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2019 at 500 billion yen.
In July, China imposed a 25 percent import tariff on U.S. soybeans in response to Washington’s moves in trade frictions.
â€œOur grain business has been hit by U.S.-China trade frictions,â€ Maruhong's chief financial officer said.
He said that Gao Hong has stopped the financial transactions of his own account since September.
Gao Hong's spokesman Pat Burke said in a statement on Friday that the company's move was "in accordance with internal policy restrictions and due to the lack of market opportunities."
He also said that the suspension of financial transactions will not lead to fewer jobs.
Maruben maintained an annual profit forecast of 230 billion yen unchanged, which was helped by the pulp and paper and power generation business.
Sumitomo Corporation reported a 16% profit increase between April and September on Thursday, stressing that "U.S. trade issues with China have led to unclear prospects."
Mitsubishi raised its annual profit forecast to record levels on Friday due to an increase in coking coal production and higher prices for commodities such as oil and coal.
Mitsubishi Corporation also announced a new business plan, aiming to increase profits from this year's estimate of 64 billion yen ($7.98 billion) for the fiscal year ending March 31, 2022.
Comprehensive report, the U.S. midterm elections vote has entered the countdown.
On November 4th, President Donald Trump and his Democratic opponents actively urged their core voters.
Both parties have pointed out that the voter turnout will be the key to left and right.
According to reports, 48 hours before the U.S. popular vote, Trump was busy attending the Republican candidate's campaign, and former President Barack Obama went to Indiana to stand for Joe Donnelly, the Democratic Senate candidate who was worried about the election, and shouted to the masses for the final appeal before the election.
On Nov. 4, Mr. Trump went to Meigang, Georgia, for Brian Kemp, the Republican gubernatorial candidate, and said, “You’ve got to go to the polling place on Tuesday, you’ve got to vote.”
"It's impossible to be clearer in the comparison of this election."
Voters’ political fervours rose to a rare peak, and early voting in some states was far ahead of usual.
As successive U.S. presidents face their first midterm elections, members of his party tend to have fewer members of Congress.
According to a new poll released by the Washington Post and ABC News on the 4th, although the Democratic House of Representatives still maintains an advantage, Republicans can benefit from the economic assessment and Trump's strict focus on border security.
Polls show that registered voters prefer Democratic House candidates more than Republicans, up from 50 percent to 43 percent, but are still down from a 14-percentage-point lead in August.
In a separate poll conducted by NBC and The Wall Street Journal, Democrats are still seven percentage points ahead of Republicans.
It is reported that Obama told the masses on the occasion of Senator Donnelly: "When people don't tell the truth, when words don't represent anything anymore, there will inevitably be bad results.
Democracy does not work when people lie to themselves.”
“The only way these Republicans can stop their behavior now is you and your vote.”
Democrats are facing the most difficult elections in the Senate in decades, and Republicans currently hold more than half of 51 seats.
However, the House election is more favorable, and Democrats need to win another 23 seats to control the 435-seat House of Representatives.
According to analysts who predicted the election website FiveThirtyEight.com, there is an 85% chance that Democrats will win the House of Representatives.
The CPPCC held an important theoretical seminar of General Secretary Xi Jinping on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC Wang Yang to attend and speak.
From the 29th to the 30th, the CPPCC National Committee held an important theoretical seminar of General Secretary Xi Jinping on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC in Beijing.
The Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the chairman of the CPPCC National People's Political Consultative Conference attended the meeting and spoke.
He stressed that General Secretary Xi Jinping's important ideas on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC have profoundly clarified the status role, goals and tasks, responsibilities and tasks and practical requirements of the CPPCC, scientifically answered a series of directional, overall and strategic major questions, which is a powerful ideological weapon guiding the work of the CPPCC in the new era.
It is necessary to earnestly study and implement this important idea, grasp its great significance, rich connotation and spiritual essence, earnestly work hard in learning and understanding, promote the quality improvement of the work of the CPPCC with theoretical learning and ideological arming, and earnestly assume the new mission of the CPPCC in the new era.
From September 29th to 30th, the CPPCC held an important theoretical seminar of General Secretary Xi Jinping on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC in Beijing.
Wang Yang pointed out that since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, General Secretary Xi Jinping has put forward a series of new ideas and new opinions on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC, for the first time that the CPPCC is an important channel for socialist consultative democracy and a special consultative body, is an important part of the national governance system, is an institutional arrangement with Chinese characteristics, for the first time to clarify the characteristics and advantages of the new party system, emphasizing the correct handling of consistency and diversity.
Wang Yang stressed that the CPPCC at all levels should take theoretical learning and discussion as an opportunity to further find the weak links and shortcomings in the work of the CPPCC, work hard to strengthen and improve, and seek breakthroughs.
It is necessary to comprehensively strengthen the construction of the CPPCC system party and ensure that the decision-making and deployment of the Party Central Committee are fully implemented into the work of the CPPCC.
It is necessary to strengthen ideological and political guidance, improve the system, procedures and mechanisms for the "two-way development" of advice and governance and consensus-building, and implement ideological and political guidance into all aspects and the whole process of performing their duties.
It is necessary to focus on the central task of performing responsibilities, better obey the overall situation of serving the party and the state, improve the quality of advice and administration, and enhance the effectiveness of performing their duties.
It is necessary to strengthen the construction of the CPPCC itself, grasp the education and training of members and cadres, give full play to the basic role of the special committee, and consolidate the foundation for the CPPCC to perform its duties.
It is necessary to strengthen the guidance of the work of the local CPPCC, take the direction, do demonstrations, solve difficult problems, and improve the overall level of CPPCC work.
In order to deeply study and implement Xi Jinping's socialist ideas with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the spirit of the Nineteenth National Congress of the Party, the CPPCC system began to carry out General Secretary Xi Jinping's important ideological learning and discussion activities on strengthening and improving the work of the CPPCC in May, held 8 regional symposiums and seven expert and scholar's seminars, identified 18 key topics and 6 basic theoretical topics.
BEIJING, Nov. 5 (Wang Xiaoyan) Under the current wave of "public entrepreneurship and innovation", more and more technology companies have begun to pay attention to patent research and development and related protection work, digging deep into the potential value of patents and occupying market dominance.
Similarly, there are many technology companies that have encountered a lot of violations in the licensing of patented technologies and the use of patented technologies.
At the end of 2017, Tan Wei, He Zhanghong and Lai Bin from Guangdong Province sued the Guangdong Pacific Internet Information Service Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Guangdong Pacific Internet Information Service Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Guangdong Pacific) to the Guangzhou Intellectual Property Court by the developers of "Didi Travel" APP on the grounds of patent infringement.
The three plaintiffs asked the court to order, and the three defendants immediately stopped manufacturing, selling, promising sales, and using the plaintiff's patent behavior.
On October 30, 2018, the China Refering Documents Network announced the first-instance civil ruling on infringement of invention patent rights disputes such as Tan Wei, He Zhanghong and Beijing Xiaoqing Technology Co., Ltd., disclosing the details of some of the cases in which the Didi Travel APP was sued for patent infringement.
The three plaintiffs believe that the patentee and the inventor of the patent based on the mobile terminal's ride-sharing service system and methods, and the entire operation process of the application of the "windmill" application in the "Didi Travel" APP corresponds to the technical solution of the patent protection involved, which constitutes patent infringement.
However, during the court's ruling, Orange Technology believes that Guangdong Pacific is not a qualified defendant, which only provides a free download of the APP "Didi Travel" involved on the network, and does not implement the patented methods involved, there are no direct or indirect infringements, and should not be listed as a defendant in this case.
Secondly, the infringement in this case is not in Guangdong.
According to the law, the infringement of the patent involved should be the location of the complete implementation of the patent method involved in the case, so it raised objections to the jurisdiction of the court and requested that the case be transferred to the court of the defendant's domicile, that is, the Beijing Intellectual Property Court.
The Guangzhou Intellectual Property Court held that it was not wrong for the defendant Guangdong Pacific to provide the allegedly infringing Didi Travel APP products on its online platform, and the plaintiff listed the defendant Guangdong Pacific as a defendant.
And the defendant Guangdong Pacific residence in Guangzhou, belongs to the jurisdiction of the Guangzhou Intellectual Property Court.
The defendant Xiaoqing Technology advocated that the case should be transferred to the Beijing Intellectual Property Court for trial, on the basis of insufficient basis, rejected the objections raised by Defendant Orange Technology Co., Ltd. to the jurisdiction of this case, and bear the cost of accepting the jurisdictional objection case.
At present, other trials of the case have not yet been announced, and the reporter will pay close attention to the follow-up details of Didi Travel's patent infringement case.
Interview with the CEO of the Australian Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organization: the results of Australia-China scientific and technological cooperation are remarkable
"China's science and technology has developed rapidly in the past few decades, and Australia and China can achieve fruitful results together in the field of science."
Larry Marshall, CEO of the Australian Federal Scientific and Industrial Research Organization, said in an interview with the China News Agency in Beijing recently that from the cooperation on climate change to the "Heavenly Eye" project, Australia-China cooperation in the field of science and technology has shown vitality.
As the largest national scientific research institution in the Commonwealth of Australia, CSIRO has achieved many innovative research results that have attracted the attention of the world in the fields of oceans, energy, biology, materials and astronomy.
CSIRO has maintained close cooperative relations with scientific research institutions such as the Chinese Academy of Sciences.
“It’s an enduring friendship that embraces a tradition of trust and long-term cooperation with partners,” Marshall said.
In May of this year, China's 500-meter-caliber spherical radio telescope, "China's Tianyin", installed the world's first 19-beam L-band receiver.
At present, the world's most advanced 19-beam feeder is jointly developed by Chinese and Australian scientists.
Marshall said that the successful development of the receiver is based on CSIRO's many years of technical accumulation, after the introduction, the FAST survey speed will be increased by 5 to 6 times, at the same time, it will also expand more scientific observation targets.
â€œThis is one of CSIRO's contributions to FAST.â€
In addition to the above-mentioned cooperation, CSIRO also cooperates closely with Chinese scientific research institutions in the construction of square kilometers of array radio telescopes, the development of new fuel technologies, and energy conservation and emission reduction.
"In the past, scientific research often focused on hundreds of years of problems, and now more scientific research is needed to solve the problems in front of us."
Marshall believes that Australia and China are complementary in the field of scientific development, and both countries are facing a series of challenges in development.
For example, extreme weather is frequent around the world, droughts and floods have led to reduced food production, and food shortages have seriously affected human development.
At the same time, population explosion, aging, chronic diseases and other issues are also serious challenges.
"The cooperation between Australia and China in recent years is mainly aimed at solving these current problems."
According to Marshall, CSIRO and the Qingdao National Laboratory of Marine Science and Technology jointly established the International Center for Marine Research in the Southern Hemisphere, its focus is to observe the El Niño phenomenon and La Niña phenomenon, study the relationship between the two and extreme weather, and establish an early warning facility for extreme weather; CSIRO and the Chinese Academy of Sciences jointly developed new varieties of grains to overcome extreme weather, can also alleviate the food shortage caused by extreme weather.
"In the current environment, scientific and technological innovation is very difficult to complete alone, requires extremely high costs, there are many problems to be solved, so cooperation is particularly important today."
Marshall said that the closer the cooperation, the more likely it is to make a breakthrough, which is also the significance of strengthening cooperation between Australia and China under the "Belt and Road" framework.
"Strengthening bilateral cooperation, for us is mainly scientific and technological cooperation."
For example, CSIRO has recently developed a gold purification method that does not use cyanide, because the traditional cyanide gold purification method is very harmful to the environment, and many countries hope to find a way to purify gold with small environmental pollution.
"We are willing to introduce this technology to China, which is one of the achievements of our participation in the 'Belt and Road' cooperation."
On the 29th, 2018, Baoji and Silk Road tourism promotion and project cooperation meeting was held in Urumqi, Xinjiang, and the participating guests could also enjoy local cuisine and feel the local heavy history and culture while appreciating the development achievements of Baoji.
In the first month of this event, Baoji successively carried out a series of high-density and large-scale tourism publicity and promotion activities in eight cities along the Silk Road, such as Tianshui, Pingliang, Lanzhou, Yinchuan, Guyuan, Xining, Zhangye and Hami, laying a good foundation for the success of the 2018 Baoji and Silk Road tourism promotion and project cooperation talks.
According to the mayor of Baoji City, Shaanxi Province, Baojie has a long history and culture, with a strong industrial foundation, and is the second largest city in Shaanxi Province and the sub-central city of Guantian Economic Zone and Guanzhong Plain urban agglomeration, and an important node city along the "Belt and Road" initiative.
In recent years, Baoji City has continuously improved the five functions of industrial clusters, logistics hubs, comprehensive services, open highlands, and cultural cohesion, so as to accelerate the promotion of catch-up and high-quality development.
At the meeting, Baoji City Tourism Development Committee and the Urumqi Tourism Bureau signed a strategic cooperation agreement on tourism between the two places.
At the same time, a number of travel agencies in Xinjiang have signed tourism cooperation agreements with Baoji Dashuichuan Tourism Scenic Spots, Famen Temple Buddhist Cultural Scenic Spots, Taibai Mountain Tourist Scenic Spots, and Guanshan Prairie Scenic Spots.
Baoji Tourism Commission market promotion section chief Chen Hongwei said: "Damei Xinjiang, some of the tourism resources and Baoji forming complementary, we all the way, to promote tourism to Xinjiang, mainly introduced the humanities Baoji, food chicken, natural scenery, etc., selected more than 500 photos, so that merchants feel the beautiful scenery of Baoji."
This event Baoji focuses on tourism resources, tourism projects, tourism routes, etc. Through the broadcasting of tourism promotional videos, the promotion of cultural tourism resources and projects, the exhibition of tourism photographic works, the production of promotional exhibitions, the issuance of promotional materials, and the docking of tourism cooperation and exchanges, it comprehensively promotes the overall image of Baoji tourism, high-quality tourism products and high-quality tourism industry projects, consolidates the source market in Xinjiang.
Feng Xu, deputy director of Baoji Investment Bureau, said: "At this event, various departments at all levels in Baoji City, counties and districts, and various development zones actively met and negotiated, and coordinated the implementation of a large number of good projects and major projects.
Up to now, a total of 41 signed projects have been implemented, involving a total amount of 26.043 billion yuan.
In recent years, around the goal of building international cities along the "Belt and Road" initiative, equipment manufacturing cities, historical and cultural cities and livable and livable beautiful and happy cities, Baoji has continuously improved the five functions of industrial clusters, logistics hubs, comprehensive services, open highlands, and cultural cohesion, and accelerated the promotion of catch-up and high-quality development.
In 2017, the gross regional product reached 218 billion yuan, an increase of 8.7%.
It has won more than 20 state-level honors such as the National Civilized City, the National Ecological Garden City and the China Habitat Environment Award.
According to the Standing Committee of the Urumqi Municipal Party Committee and Deputy Mayor Yan Naimin, Urumqi, as the key town of New North Road on the Silk Road, has special geographical geographical advantages, connecting the north and south of Tianshan since ancient times, communicating between Xinjiang and the mainland, and passing through an important channel between China and Central Asia, West Asia and Europe, which is an important window for China's opening to the west and economic and cultural exchanges to the outside world.
This event focuses on equipment manufacturing, logistics commerce, and tourism industry, and shines in Urumqi with the sincerity of seeking good opportunities for development and consultation and cooperation plans.
At the meeting, local merchants in Xinjiang signed six projects with Baoji counties and districts, involving an amount of 3.25 billion yuan.
On the same day, representatives of Kyrgyzstan's visa office in Urumqi, representatives of Russia's Novosibirsk Law Co., Ltd., Tajik Chamber of Commerce and Industry in Urumqi, representatives of the Russian Tatarstan Chamber of Commerce attended the meeting.
About 500 people participated in the talks between Urumqi China Merchants Bureau, Commerce Bureau, Agriculture and Animal Husbandry Bureau, Tourism Bureau and other departments, enterprises, and the media.
The revitalization of the northeast is related to the overall situation of national development.
Industrial enterprises in the northeast region are better than major and basic, for the northeast, to grasp innovation is to grasp development, and to seek innovation is to seek the future.
Whether the vitality of the old industrial base can be re-energized and released, affecting the heart of the general secretary.
North Korea's foreign affairs minister told the United Nations on Saturday that continuing to impose sanctions has deepened North Korea's distrust of the United States, and it is impossible for North Korea to unilaterally give up nuclear weapons under such circumstances.
At the United Nations General Assembly, Mr. Lee said North Korea had taken a “very friendly approach” over the past year, including halting missile and nuclear tests, dismantling nuclear test sites, and promising non-proliferation of nuclear weapons and technology.
“But we haven’t seen any corresponding response from the U.S.,” he said.
"If we don't trust the United States, there will be no confidence in our national security, and under such circumstances, we can't unilaterally give up weapons first."
While Mr. Ryong-ho is repeating North Korea’s complaints that the U.S. opposes “phased” denuclearization, his speech is of great significance, because there is no complete rejection of unilateral denuclearisation, as North Korea has done in the past.
Mr. Li referred to a June 12 joint statement by Mr. Kim and Mr. Trump, who agreed to work toward “denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula,” while Mr. Trump pledged to protect North Korea’s security.
North Korea has always sought to formally end the 1950-53 Korean War, but the United States says North Korea must give up its nuclear weapons first.
The U.S. has also refused to ease demands for international sanctions against North Korea.
â€œThe United States insists on â€œdenuclearizing firstâ€ and increases the pressure on sanctions, achieves its goal in a high-pressure manner, and even refuses to issue a â€œDeclaration on the End of Warâ€ ,â€ Li Yonghao said.
"The idea that sanctions can make us knelt for forgiveness is that people who don't understand us are daydreaming."
But the problem is that such ongoing sanctions are deepening our distrust.”
Li did not mention the US president's plan for the second summit at the United Nations earlier this week.
Instead, he highlighted three meetings between Kim and South Korean President Moon Jae-in over the past five months, saying: “If the other side of denuclearization is South Korea, not North Korea, then denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula will not become so rigid.”
China announced that it will reduce import tariffs on 1,585 tax items from November 1, 2018.
Since the beginning of this year, China has successively taken the initiative to reduce import tariffs.
On May 1 this year, the comprehensive tax reduction of drugs, including all ordinary drugs of anti-cancer drugs and alkaloid drugs with anti-cancer effects, actual imports of traditional Chinese medicine, a total of 28 tax items to adjust the import price adjustment is zero.
At the same time, it also significantly reduces the value-added tax burden on the production and import of anti-cancer drugs.
On July 1, taxes were reduced on cars and parts for 218 tax items.
After the tax reduction, China's automobile vehicle tax rate has been lower than the average level of developing countries, in line with the reality of China's automobile industry.
This tax reduction will promote the adjustment of the industry structure and optimize the allocation of resources, accelerate the survival of the fittest, and help improve the quality of products and services, which is expected to promote the adjustment of automobile prices to a certain extent, so that consumers can get more benefits.
On July 1, taxes were reduced on daily consumer goods for 1,449 tax items.
The tax reduction of daily consumer goods is closely related to the people's needs for a better life.
This tax reduction is not only large but also strong, with an average tax reduction rate of 56%.
The reduction of taxes on daily consumer goods will directly benefit the majority of consumers and promote the competitiveness of domestic industries.
On November 1st, taxes will be implemented for industrial products such as mechanical and electrical equipment, spare parts and raw materials for 1,585 tax items.
Properly reducing the import tariffs on industrial products that are in urgent need in some countries can attract more foreign investment, which is conducive to increasing effective domestic supply, helping industrial upgrading, while helping enterprises allocate resources around the world, reduce production costs, and also reduce the pressure on the domestic environment.
According to the relevant person in charge of the Office of the Customs Tariff Commission of the State Council of the People's Republic of China, the above four independent tax cuts, as well as the third step of the implementation of the implementation of the results of the expanded negotiations under the information technology agreement on July 1 this year, will reduce China's total tariff level from 9.8% in the previous year to 7.5%.
The overall adjusted tariff level is slightly higher than that of the European Union, lower than that of most developing countries, and is at a moderately low level, which basically matches the status and development stage of developing countries in China.
As one of the important indicators of China's openness in the field of goods trade, the total level of tariffs should adapt to China's economic development stage and reflect the characteristics of the times.
China's trade in goods is the first in the world, and it already has the economic foundation for further opening up, but there is still a gap between the quality and efficiency of trade development and developed economies, so the overall level of tariffs should be appropriately reduced.
Tariffs are a means of protecting compliance, tariff levels should be compatible with industrial competitiveness, to encourage healthy competition, excessive protection is not conducive to industrial development and improvement of quality.
The adjustment of the tariff rate should take into account the needs of production and consumer demand.
Focus on reducing commodity tax rates with greater domestic demand, which is conducive to industrial transformation and upgrading, and strive to increase the import of distinctive and advantageous products where the needs of the people are relatively concentrated, and constantly enhance the sense of acquisition of enterprises and the public, and meet the needs of upgrading the industrial structure and consumption structure.
The reduction of taxes should take into account the affordability of fiscal revenue and industrial development.
In the selection of specific tax reduction commodities and tax reduction, it is necessary to coordinate the relationship between the two domestic and foreign markets, the upstream and downstream two aspects, and production and consumption, so as to maintain China's steady development momentum.
The person in charge stressed that this year is the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up, and China's initiative to reduce the overall level of import tariffs is based on China's own major measures to achieve high-quality development needs, which is conducive to the overall utilization of international and foreign resources, promote the quality improvement of the domestic supply system, and meet the needs of the people's consumption and upgrading.
Such actions and measures show that China will unswervingly adhere to a mutually beneficial and win-win opening-up strategy, firmly support economic globalization, resolutely safeguard the principle of free trade and the multilateral trading system with the WTO as the core, continue to draw development momentum from opening up to the world, and let China's development better benefit the world.
Serbia has announced that it has entered the highest state of readiness, and the President of Serbia and Russia will meet tomorrow to discuss the situation in Kosovo.
According to the office of the President of Serbia, President Vučić has ordered that the country's armed forces have entered the highest state of readiness in view of the occupation by Kosovo special forces of the Gazivoda Hydropower Station, which is controlled by Belgrade in the north of Kosovo.
On September 29, the Serbian Minister of Defense, Vulin, announced that the Serbian army had entered a state of full combat readiness.
Vulin stressed that as long as Vučić's order is still valid, Serbia will continue to monitor the current situation in Kosovo, regardless of the direction of the situation, the Serbian army will respond.
According to Russia's TASS news agency, Vucic said in an interview on September 29 that he has informed the current situation with all parties such as the United States, Russia and Europe, and will go to Moscow on October 2 to meet with Russian President Putin to seek Putin's support on the Kosovo issue.
Asked if Serbia needed Russian military support like Syria, Vuččić replied: "I don't want a major military conflict on our territory."
Vučić also said that Serbian forces entering a state of full combat readiness were only intended to form a deterrent to prevent the conflict from occurring, but it was also a clear warning that there would never be tolerance of any violence in Kosovo.
The reason why the Serb army has increased its combat readiness is related to two major moves on the side of Kosovo.
According to the Serbian side, in recent days, Albanians are aggressively arresting ethnic Serbs living there for generations in northern Kosovo, and these arrested Serbs have not violated any laws.
Vučić said that since March 26 this year, the head of the Serbian government offices in Kosovo and Metohija, Mako Yurić, was beaten and detained by the Kosovo Albanian army, the Albanians have escalated the situation in the region and carried out inhumane arrests and evictions of Serbs.
In addition, more than 100 people, including the ROSU special forces, armed police and snipers of the Ministry of Internal Affairs of the Republic of Kosovo, which recently announced the establishment, occupied positions in the vicinity of the Gazivoda Hydropower Plant, entered the ecological and sports center near the levee in the northern part of Kosovo, and blocked all nearby roads, which were originally controlled by the Serbian side.
Vučić pointed out that this military adventure in Kosovo was carried out at the instigation of Western countries, and the action of the Kosovo army did not inform the Serbian side in advance, in violation of Chapter IX, paragraph 1, of the Brussels Agreement, as well as a violation of UN Security Council resolution 1244 and the military-technical agreement between Serbia and Serbia.
Vučić has spoken to NATO Secretary-General Stoltenberg, criticizing the hypocrisy of Western countries on the issue of Kosovo.
At the root of the current conflict is still the centuries-old feud between the Serbs in Kosovo.
With regard to the ownership of Kosovo, Serbs and ethnic Albanians have their own statements.
Serbia regarded Kosovo as the birthplace of the nation and the cradle of culture, because Serbia established its most powerful country here in the 12th century, and the Albanians only moved in large quantities after the Ottoman invasion and the defeat of the Serbian army in the north.
Albanians, for their part, insisted that the primordial tribe of the Illyrians living in Kosovo in the 4-5th century B.C. were the ancestors of ethnic Albanians, so Kosovo has been the territory of ethnic Albanians since ancient times.
Subjective political divisions have led to intense conflicts between different nationalities, religions and cultures, resulting in fierce confrontations between Serbs and Albanians in Kosovo.
In 1912, Kosovo Albanians first proclaimed the independence of Albania.
After the First World War, a large number of ethnic Albanians living in the Balkans moved to Turkey, and the proportion of Serbs increased relatively, and in the view of the Serbs, the practice of "only taking back their own land" was regarded by Albanians as the plundering of "Greater Serbianism".
Kosovo has become the "powder barrel" of the Balkans.
In 1999, armed clashes between Albanian separatists in the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA) and the Serbian army and police led to the bombing of the Federal Republic of Serbia and Montenegro and the outbreak of the war in Kosovo.
On February 17, 2008, Kosovo unilaterally declared its independence from Serbia.
Although there is news that Serbia will normalize relations with Kosovo and sign a global and legally binding agreement, due to historical ethnic grievances and geopolitical constraints, an agreement that is subject to multiple forces such as the United States, Europe and Russia has not been able to be signed.
Just a month ago, Vučić made it clear for the first time that he advocated the isolation of Serbs and Albanians in Kosovo, and once again publicized the contradictions between the two communities.
Electricity communication is still interrupted, and Indonesia's strong earthquake and tsunami relief are difficult.
According to figures released by the Indonesian Disaster Relief Agency in the early morning of the 30th, a strong earthquake and caused tsunami in Donggara County in the country's Central Sulawesi Province on the 28th have killed 420 people.
Wilem Rampangilei, head of Indonesia's disaster relief agency, said that the figure is only a preliminary figure in the city of Palu in the central province of Sulawesi, about 80 kilometers from the epicenter, because of the lack of large-scale search and rescue machinery, many hotels, shopping malls, warehouses and other densely populated buildings damaged by the collapse of the city have not yet been searched and rescued.
On September 29, 2018 local time, a bridge damaged by an earthquake and tsunami collapsed into several knots.
Due to the severe damage to electricity and communications facilities, the epicentre of the epicentry of Dongala Prefecture and the neighboring Siji area is still an "island" that cannot be contacted, and it is impossible to count the number of victims.
According to media reports, Indonesia's Vice President Kalla said that the death toll may reach thousands.
Disruption of electricity, interruption of communications, disruption of roads, damage to the airport . . . rescue efforts after the earthquake and tsunami were difficult.
Due to power outages, some hospitals and rescue settlements in Palu City need to rely on fuel for power generation.
Roads into and out of the city were blocked by landslides, and large transport vehicles, including tanker trucks, were unable to enter, making fuel supplies very tight.
Indonesia's Minister of Social Affairs Agus said that due to road damage, tents, mattresses, blankets, clothing, food and household goods bags and other emergency disaster relief materials transferred by the Ministry from South Sulawesi and Corentalo provinces in the vicinity of the earthquake area have not yet arrived in the disaster area.
Disaster relief materials transferred from the capital Jakarta are being transported to the affected areas by air transport aircraft.
In view of the damage caused by the observation tower and runway at Palu airport during the earthquake, in order to ensure safety and rescue, all commercial flights have been suspended, and military aircraft carrying relief supplies and personnel have only taken off and landed.
Indonesia's political, legal and security affairs co-ordinating minister who commanded the rescue in the earthquake area called for the resumption of power supply and commercial flight services at the airport as soon as possible to ensure the operation of rescue agencies such as hospitals, so that more rescuers, volunteers, and aid materials can arrive in the affected areas.
On the 28th, a number of strong earthquakes occurred in Donggala County, Central Sulawesi Province, Indonesia, among which a 7.7-magnitude strong earthquake occurred at 17:02 local time caused a tsunami, resulting in a major disaster in Palu City, Dongala County, and Xiji District.
BEIJING, Oct. 1 (Reporter Yin Li) Like washing, clear skies, and full skies... Recently, Beijing has continued to open the most beautiful blue sky model, attracting thousands of people in Beijing on the social station fancy show, in the continuous swiping of happiness, said "under the blue sky and white clouds, 'drunk' skyline, this is Beijing's best business card."
Since August, Beijing has ushered in the "bluest sky".
In Beijing, you can see the public anytime, anywhere or holding a smartphone, or holding a SLR camera to take pictures.
On social platforms such as Weibo, WeChat circle of friends, you can see the Forbidden City, Tian'an Gate, Bird's Nest, Hutong in the netizen lens... All kinds of buildings show a different beauty under the blue sky.
Some netizens said that such a "scenery blockbuster" is Beijing's best urban propaganda film; some netizens ridiculed that if such a blue sky is long-swiped, people with cervical spondylosis can be cured; more netizens hope that "this smear can overwinter spring and summer, so that Beijing's sky screen is blue in the four seasons."
Why do people in Chicago love the blue sky?
Just because the people living in this city in the past are suffering from smog, so they are particularly eager for the blue sky, and launched the "blue sky defense war" in Beijing, after the continuous improvement of air quality, smog becomes less, the blue sky increases, the people are happy in their eyes, and the happiness obtained is particularly heavy.
On the day of the National Day, the weather in Beijing was fine.
At 8 a.m., the vast majority of the city's 35 air quality monitoring sites were shown as "first-class excellent" green.
On the social platform by the people's spontaneous "bluest sky" themed photo contest is still continuing.
Why is the sky in Beijing so blue lately?
According to the relevant person in charge of the Beijing Municipal Environmental Protection Bureau, in August this year, the average concentration of fine particulate matter (PM2.5) in Beijing was 35 micrograms per cubic meter, setting the best record for the same period in the history of nearly five years.
The real-time concentration of PM2.5 in September is more frequent in single digits.
One of the major factors in the emergence of the "bluest sky" is the overall favorable meteorological conditions in recent times, and more importantly, Beijing has persistently carried out air pollution control, vigorously promoted the clean air action plan in the past five years, and the continuous release of environmental benefits has reduced the total amount of pollutant emissions in the region, which laid the foundation for the continuous improvement of air quality.
In 2013, Beijing officially released and implemented the Beijing Clean Air Action Plan 2013-2017.
According to the plan, officials continue to guide non-capital functional dredging, and promote clean energy substitution and polluting and emission reduction, eliminating a total of 4,923 coal-fired boilers.
As a result, Beijing has also become the first major city in mainland China to realize the natural gasization of the entire network.
According to the data, between 2013 and 2017, the average annual concentration of PM2.5 in Beijing decreased by 35.6%; the number of air quality days increased by 50 days; the number of first-class best days increased by 25 days; the number of heavy pollution days was reduced by 35 days, and the incidence of heavy pollution was significantly reduced.
At the same time of continuous improvement in air quality, according to the analysis of a new round of PM2.5 sources, Beijing officially released the "Three-year Action Plan for Winning the Blue Sky Defense War in Beijing" in September this year, in view of the current stage of governance and pollution characteristics, focusing on key prevention and control areas such as diesel trucks, dust, and volatile organic compounds, optimizing the adjustment of transportation structure, industrial structure, energy structure and land use structure, strengthening regional joint prevention and control, focusing on strengthening urban fine management, comprehensively promoting green development.
During this year's National Day Golden Week, relevant departments such as the Municipal Tourism Commission, industry and commerce, urban management, and public security will strengthen the law enforcement inspection of the "one-day tour" market, focusing on the chaos of "six blacks" in tourism, and once those who violate the law are verified, they will be severely and severely punished in accordance with the law.
Yesterday morning, the municipal government held a special meeting to crack down on illegal "one-day tour" and deployed special actions to further crack down on illegal "one-day travel".
At the meeting, it was revealed that focusing on the "six black" chaos of black tickets, black guides, black agencies, black cars, black shops, and black network interest chains, the city has launched a special action to crack down on illegal "one-day tours" since July 28.
So far, the city has accepted a total of 39 complaints of "one-day travel", down 63% year-on-year; this year, the city has accepted 270 complaints of "day trips", down 62% year-on-year.
In the past two months, the city seized 248 sets of "black cars", investigated and punished 158 cases of tourism passenger traffic violations, closed 29 shopping "black shops" and performing arts venues, investigated and dealt with 13 "black clubs", "black guides" 27 people, confiscated 26,000 illegal advertisements, dismantled 31 illegal "day travel" billboards, 3 bus fake station cards, investigated and punished all kinds of travel-related illegal acts 1789, all functional departments filed 181 cases, from a heavy fine of 4.
After rectification, illegal "one-day travel" chaos has basically been curbed, and the market order of "day trip" has shown a stable and positive trend.
According to reports, in recent years, the city has continuously increased its efforts to rectify the illegal "day trip".
In 2016 and 2017, the Municipal Tourism Commission accepted 1,612 and 897 complaints of â€œday tripsâ€ , a decrease of 79% and 44% year-on-year respectively, but the illegal â€œday tripâ€ is still incessant, often rebounding, and formed a "six black" chaos with intertwined interest chains such as black tickets, black guides, black agencies, black cars, black shops, and black nets.
In particular, the street illegal soliciting personnel is "black ticket", the illegal website that publishes false travel information, that is, the "black net", the travel agency engaged in the illegal "day trip" or the agency or individual without travel agency management qualification is the "black society", the "black society" hired without a touring certificate or a tour guide in violation of the practice, that is, a "black guide", the use of vehicles without tourist passenger transport qualifications or for illegal "day tour".
In this special operation, the city continued to increase the fixed inspection and mobile inspection of the illegal "day trip", in response to the illegal "day trip" high frequency and the impact of tourist routes, the relevant departments sent an unannounced visit to the car every day, found the evidence of illegal violations in accordance with the strict investigation according to law.
Among them, "black car" and "black shop" has become the focus of the two special actions.
According to reports, without black cars, illegal "one-day travel" can not travel, black cars are easy to detect, remember and deal with, but also a single fixed asset with higher value.
Relevant departments using road traffic monitoring probes to increase the supervision of key "day trip" line tourism buses, the use of technical defense, physical defense and other scientific and technological intelligent means can be found in time to investigate and deal with the "black car".
Tourism shopping "black shop" due to a small number of sitting operations, has also become the focus.
In order to strengthen the deterrence and crackdown on illegal "one-day tours", all functional departments will be severely and severely punished in accordance with the law, as soon as any violation of the law is verified in the special action.
In August this year, the city also held a seminar to crack down on illegal "day trip" related legal issues, and discussed the combination of administrative punishment and conviction.
The Municipal Tourism Commission said that in the future, it will encourage more regular travel agencies to carry out Beijing's "one-day trip" and increase the supply of regular "day tours" to further squeeze the living space of illegal "one-day tours".
In addition, the Municipal Tourism Commission has also continuously improved the electronic itinerary single information system of tour groups to ensure that each team is included in the supervision of the electronic itinerary platform.
From a tourist symbol to a digital economy symbol, what has Wuzhen experienced over the years?
As the permanent venue of the World Internet Conference, how Wuzhen can undertake the summit dividend has attracted much attention.
From the beginning of the first World Internet Conference, in the past five years, the changes in Wuzhen have been obvious to all.
In 2014, there were only 12 enterprises related to the digital economy and the Internet in the whole town, and by the third quarter of this year, there were more than 500.
This is a microcosm of the development of the digital economy in Wuzhen.
The convening of the Internet Conference allows local enterprises to accept the enlightenment of the digital economy and the wave of digitalization at zero distance, and the desire for enterprise transformation and upgrading is very strong, and traditional manufacturing enterprises have increased investment and research and development in terms of machine substitution and intelligent management.
Jiang Wei, party secretary of Wuzhen Town, said that Wuzhen will build a new economic empowerment center in the future.
The development of the digital economy is inseparable from the support of infrastructure.
This year, Wuzhen launched the 5G pilot work on the basis of achieving full coverage of 4G communication network and free WiFi.
At the same time, Tongxiang City, where Wuzhen is located, has also become a hot spot for the development of the Internet industry as the country's first county-level city to build a special channel for international Internet data.
Since the first World Internet Conference, Tongxiang has introduced a total of 565 digital economy projects, with a total planned investment of 37.725 billion yuan. In the first three quarters of this year, the core manufacturing industry of the digital economy achieved a total output value of 8.73 billion yuan, an increase of 13% year-on-year.
"Wuzhen was a tourist symbol before, and then there were more drama and cultural symbols. Because of the Internet Conference, it has now become a symbol of the Internet and the digital economy."
Sheng Yongjun, secretary of the Tongxiang Municipal Party Committee, believes that the dividends of the World Internet Conference have accumulated over time, so it is also necessary to build a platform to undertake the superimposed introduction of talents, projects, technologies and other factors from all parties.
Shen Yi worked abroad for 20 years, and returned to his hometown to start a business because of his relationship with the Internet conference.
On December 2 last year, with high-capacity tamper-proof digital technology solutions, he walked into the 4th Internet Light Expo, which was favored by many customers.
Shen Yi chose to start a business in Wuzhen not only because of the hometown complex, "in Wuzhen, it is easier to recruit people than I imagined, our application is also landing very fast, Wuzhen intelligent parking project has our application."
A Wuzhen Avenue presents the spillover effect of the Internet Conference.
This boulevard, which runs through the north and south of Tongxiang Township, is not only linked with tourist attractions, but also an industrial avenue.
Relying on it, Wuzhen Avenue Kechuang Gathering Area came into being.
The reporter learned that in the future, Wuzhen Avenue will become the main position for the development of Tongxiang's industry, taking the lead in applying a large number of achievements such as smart medical care, smart old-age care, and smart government affairs, gathering 80% of the city's GDP and many high-level talents.
Tsunami triggered by earthquake in Indonesia has killed at least 410 people.
According to the 29th night of the public information director of the Jakarta police in Indonesia, the current earthquake in Central Sulawesi Province has killed 410 people, 97 of whom have been identified.
Another 29 people are missing and 540 are injured.
Palu airport is still closed.
In active treatment, China's survival rate of preterm infants aged 29 weeks and above reached 98%, which has reached the level of developed countries.
SHANGHAI, Sept. 30 (Xinhua) -- The National Children's Medical Center and Fudan Pediatric Hospital disclosed on the 30th that they introduced Canada's advanced methods in the leading "China NICU Inpatient Premature Premature Premature Quality Improvement Project".
According to the results of the project, after active treatment, China's survival rate of preterm infants of 29 weeks and above has reached 98%, which has reached the level of developed countries, but there is still much room for improvement in the non-complication survival rate of extremely gestated and premature infants.
Over the past two decades, the Chinese government has been paying attention to the treatment of newborns.
At present, the infant mortality rate in Shanghai has dropped to 3.71 ‰, which is significantly lower than the national average and has reached the advanced level of developed countries.
"China NICU Hospital Premature Premature Premature Premature Quality Improvement Project" through four years of unremitting efforts, greatly improving the survival quality of premature infants.
Professor Cao Yun, director of the neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) of Fudan University Affiliated Pediatric Hospital, told reporters that while improving the survival rate of premature babies, we are concerned about reducing the survival quality of premature babies, reducing the incidence of complications, improving neurophaid prognosis, and improving the overall outcome of children, which is of great significance to improving the overall survival quality and population quality of premature babies.
Through four years of unremitting efforts to include tens of thousands of preterm infants aged 33 weeks and below, the mortality rate of premature babies with small gestational age and low birth weight in China has decreased by 1/3, while the incidence of serious complications of preterm infants has decreased significantly, which has greatly improved the survival quality of preterm infants.
Through the establishment of a national newborn quality improvement cooperation network and the introduction of the concept of collaborative quality improvement, the project radiates 25 collaborative hospitals across China, and establishes a complete, systematic and effective collaborative quality improvement method for improving the preterm baby's prognosis and improving the level of neonatal treatment.
Fudan University Affiliated Pediatric Hospital is working with the National Neonatology Force to develop guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of neonatal infection according to the accumulated experience of the project, so as to provide reference and guidance for the standardized diagnosis and treatment of newborn infections in China.
It is understood that in the "Premature Premature Quality Improvement Project in China", Pediatric Hospital has introduced the EPIQ method to 25 large NICUs in 19 provinces across the country, and is committed to solving the problem of preterm infant infections that plague China's neonatal monitoring units.
After more than 10 years of continuous improvement, Canada's uncomplicated survival rate of preterm babies has increased by about one-third, and Canada is now one of the countries with the best prognosis for premature babies in the world.
The EPIQ method has now been applied to all NICUs in Canada and has been applied in six countries.
Two years after EPIQ intervention, preterm infections fell by 35%, while antibiotic use fell by 20 percent.
In the future, Fudan University Affiliated Pediatric Hospital will continue to promote and implement this method nationwide, focusing on comprehensively reducing the incidence of all complications of premature babies and improving the quality of treatment for newborns nationwide.
At present, it is an indisputable fact that there are differences in the level of treatment in various regions of China and inequities.
According to Professor Cao Yun, as an important construction unit of the National Children's Medical Center, Pediatric Hospital will play a leading role in radiating, and this study covers many western provinces such as Xinjiang, Guizhou, Gansu and Shaanxi, with a view to gradually promoting the homogenization and standardization of neonatal treatment nationwide.
It is understood that Fudan University Affiliated Pediatric Hospital is working with the National Neonatology Force to develop guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of neonatal infection according to the accumulated experience of the project, so as to provide reference and guidance for the standardized diagnosis and treatment of newborn infections in China.
According to reports, in 2019, the coordination center is located in the China Newborn Collaboration Network of Fudan Pediatric Hospital, which will work with 63 hospitals across the country for the next stage of nationwide quality improvement, with a view to promoting the development of the level of neonatal treatment in China.
Wu Xianlei, director of the Shanghai Municipal Health and Family Planning Commission, said that Shanghai can become the central city of the Asian center, not only reflected in the research, the construction of the entire service system, the quality of service and service results should have a place in Asia, so as to truly reflect China's medical level.
Xin Zhiping: Building the "Heror's Monument" in his heart - written on the Fifth Martyrs' Day.
On September 30th, on the eve of the 69th birthday of the Republic, we ushered in the fifth Martyrs' Day, and Xi Jinping and other party and state leaders came to Tiananmen Square to attend the ceremony of presenting flower baskets to people's heroes.
At this moment, no matter where you are, please pay tribute to Heroes.
Remembrance is to relive, but also to wake up.
Opening up the heavy history, behind the name of every martyr, is a vivid life.
They also have fiery youth, sincere love, and concerned families.
However, because they firmly believe that "the doctrine of our faith is the truth of the universe", they are willing to sacrifice everything for the sake of "exonerating the sufferings of the next generation."
â€œIf I live one day, I'm going to shout a day for China.â€
Through time and space, the heroes set up spiritual signposts, guiding the way forward.
â€œWhere do you come from, where to go â€œWhat kind of person to be â€œWhat kind of personâ€, it’s not difficult to get the answer.
The most important thing is to build a "hero monument" in your heart.
According to incomplete statistics, since the beginning of the revolutionary war, about 20 million martyrs have died bravely for national independence, people's liberation and national prosperity.
For various reasons, many martyrs didn’t even leave names.
Countless heroes water their ideals with blood, practice their beliefs with their lives, remember their British names, and pass on their spirit, which is to protect the roots and souls of the nation.
This â€œHero Monumentâ€ does not allow any defacement and destruction.
For some time, undercurrents such as historical nihilism and pan-entertainment have surged.
All kinds of practices that distort history and demean Yingli, challenge the conscience of justice and distort value judgments, and arouse public anger and vigilance in the whole society.
Heroes can't blaspheme, heroes don't forget.
For the act of touching the bottom line, it is impossible to listen to it, and we must dare to shine the sword and defend the dignity of the glory with the rule of law and justice.
On May 1st this year, the Law on the Protection of Heroes and Martyrs officially came into force.
Judging from judicial practice, the judgment in some cases is very popular, not only to effectively maintain the glorious image of Yinglie in accordance with the law, but also to release the positive energy of advocating heroes and reverence.
There is not a pursuing nation without heroes, an ideal country can not be without pioneers.
Reminiscing the martyrs and calling for heroes has become a universal social consensus.
At present, there are millions of commemorative facilities of various types in the country, and more than 100 million people visit the Martyrs' Cemetery every year.
The human heart is the strongest cornerstone.
Let advocating heroes, defending heroes, learning heroes, and caring for heroes, so that the spirit of heroism is integrated into the national bloodline, one by one, the "hero monument" will stand between heaven and earth and the depths of people's hearts.
BRUSSELS, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The European Union took a non-confrontational stance against Italy on Friday after Italy flouted the EU’s call for a massive budget deficit to surprise markets, but the bloc may take a more aggressive stance if Italy sticks to its too bold goals.
Italy's Euroskeptic government's goal is a budget deficit equivalent to 2.4% of gross domestic product (GDP) for the next three years, indicating that there is still no debt reduction in the face of deficit reduction requirements.
"We have no interest in the crisis between the Commission and Italy," the European Commission's Economic Affairs commissar Moscovesi said on Friday. "He responded cautiously as the EU's recommendations and sanctions may have little impact on Italy."
EU officials and diplomats still hope that market forces will be able to persuade Italy to adjust its budget plan before Italy formally submits it to the European Commission in mid-October.
The euro fell to its lowest level in nearly two weeks on Friday after the government announced its plans, while Italian bond yields hit a three-week high.
If the deficit target remains unchanged by the October deadline, the European Commission may veto Italy’s draft budget, something it has never done to any country.
European Commission Vice President Dombrovski later told a meeting in the Latvian capital Riga on Friday that Italy's current fiscal plan "seems to be inconsistent with the Stability and Growth Pact," referring to the EU's fiscal rules.
But he didn’t say how it would provoke a reaction from the EU.
Bidders can submit an application to participate in this public tender by October 26 this year.
Previously, the Russian Ministry of Agriculture regarded China as one of the priority markets for Russian agricultural exports.
The Russian Agricultural Supervision Agency announced in May that Russian grain exports to China exceeded 1 million tons for the first time in this agricultural year, a new record.
The bureau predicts that China may be among the top 10 Russian grain importers.
SAPPRO, Sept. 30 (Xinhua) -- Following the first 3-0 victory over Cuba, the Chinese women's volleyball team once again defeated the Turkish team by 3:0 on the 30th, winning two consecutive wins in the 2018 world championships.
However, compared with the first battle, the Chinese women's volleyball campaign is more difficult.
A total of 24 teams participated in the 2018 Women's Volleyball World Championships, and the Chinese women's volleyball team was in Group B with Italy, Turkey, Bulgaria, Canada and Cuba.
Judging from the world rankings and overall strength of each team in Group B, Turkey and Italy are the main opponents of the Chinese team.
After the start of the game on the same day, the Chinese team entered the state quickly, and the beginning took the lead, maintaining the advantage of the whole process, giving no small pressure to the opponent in the service and blocking the Internet, and won the first game with 25:18.
In the second game into the state of the Turkish team service is very fierce, the start has achieved a 6:2 lead, the Chinese team asked for the suspension to adjust the formation, and gradually chased the score to 7 levels, and then repeatedly blocked the net score, played 7:0 scoring tide; at the end of the game, the Turkish team once chased the score to 15:19; the Chinese team at the end of 24:20 to get the point, the tenacious Turkish team chased 2 points; the Chinese team once again called for suspension.
The situation in the third game is very glued, and the scores of the two sides have alternately risen, and at one point, it reached 19 levels.
At the crucial moment, the Turkish team made mistakes, the Chinese team led by 21:19, and with Zhu Ting's strong deduction and Zhang Changning's attack to 24:21 won the match point; then the Turkish team chased the score to 23:24, after the Chinese team asked to be suspended, Zhang Changning attacked and scored, and the Chinese team locked in the game with 25:23.
China women's volleyball coach Lang Ping admitted after the game that the whole game was not easy.
"We are prepared to be more adequate, the network is good, the Turkish team is more comprehensive, we have to reduce mistakes, and strive to win through our own initiative."
In the face of familiar teammates in the past, Zhu Ting, who played for Turkey's Wakifo Bank team, was subject to many restrictions in the first game of the day's game, and then she took the initiative to change, and still played a strong attack.
â€œAnd the opponents are very familiar with each other, and it is very normal to be targeted by the opponent, but the Chinese team played to the extreme, in the case of a bad pass, the network and the attack played very well.â€
Next, the Chinese women's volleyball team will be truced one day for physical fitness and technical training; on October 2, they will face Canada, the third opponent in the group stage.
Hengshui, September 30 (Cui Zhiping Wang Peng) On the 30th, Hengshui High-tech Zone in Hebei Province held a centralized construction ceremony for key projects in the second half of 2018.
On the same day, six projects were concentrated, with a total investment of 4.29 billion yuan.
On the same day, Hengshui Municipal Party Committee Standing Committee and Deputy Mayor Yang Shikun announced the start of construction.
According to Yao Happiness, director of the Hengshui High-tech Zone Management Committee in Hebei Province, the six projects that started today, with a total investment of 4.29 billion yuan, are all industrial projects, including the transformation and upgrading of traditional industries and the cultivation and introduction of emerging industries, covering military-civilian integration, cloud factories, food, medicine, chemicals and other industries.
It is believed that the construction and commissioning of these projects will surely inject strong impetus into the goal of "construction of hundreds of billion-level industrial parks and striving to create national-level high-tech zones" in high-tech zones in advance.
Hengshui Municipal Party Committee Standing Committee, Deputy Mayor Yang Shikun announced the start of the project.
Yao said that the district has successfully carried out a series of major activities such as the China Hengshui International Life Sciences Summit and the Great Health Industry Development Forum, the Hengshui Summit of Academicians of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, and the "double collaboration" innovation forum of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei in 2018, vigorously developing three strategic emerging industries of new material energy, big health and high-end equipment manufacturing.
The China-U.S. stem cell project will be officially put into operation by the end of the year
Zhongke vanadium and titanium all-in-one-ton pilot base, the country's first, the world's largest megawatt supercritical carbon dioxide compressor experimental platform began construction.
Compulsory ability among the world's top ten Xiongan (Hengshui) advanced supercomputing center has been approved by the provinces and cities for construction.
Yao said that by the end of the year, the district will complete 240,000 square meters of science and technology valley second major projects such as digital information, new energy and new materials, three research and development bases for life and health and display centers.
It will actively build an "upgraded version" of the "Chinese Academy of Sciences +" innovation model, build "two houses, one platform and one base", and promote the integration and innovation of scientific and technological achievements through interdisciplinary, multi-unit collaboration and multi-industry integration.
Nearly a thousand state-owned scenic spots have lowered their ticket prices by more than half, down more than 20%.
As of September 28, 981 scenic spots have been implemented or released to the public free opening or price reduction measures (74 free openings, 907 price reductions), Yunnan Shilin, Dali Three Towers, Yulong Snow Mountain, Guangxi Guilin Lijiang, Fujian Wuyi Mountain, Hunan Zhangjiajijie, Shaanxi soldiers and horses, Jiangxi Sanqing Mountain, Xinjiang Kanas and other scenic spots have implemented price cuts.
In order to implement the decision-making and deployment of the Central Economic Work Conference and the "Government Work Report", the National Development and Reform Commission issued the "Guiding Opinions on Improving the Ticket Price Formation Mechanism of State-owned Scenic Spots to Reduce Ticket Prices in Key State-owned Scenic Spots" (hereinafter referred to as "Guiding Opinions") on June 28, requiring them to improve the ticket price formation mechanism of state-owned scenic spots from the aspects of reasonably defining ticket pricing costs, innovative price management methods, and strict implementation of pricing procedures.
In accordance with the deployment requirements, all localities have actively carried out their work, and have successively reduced the ticket prices of a number of key state-owned scenic spots.
As of September 28th, 981 scenic spots have been implemented or issued to the public free opening or price reduction measures (74 free open, 907), of which 159 5A-level scenic spots, 534 4A scenic spots, a total of 693, accounting for 70.6%.
Among the 907 scenic spots that cut prices, 491 fell by more than 20%, accounting for 54.3%, down more than 30%, accounting for 23.6%.
Yunnan, Shandong, Guangxi, Shaanxi and other provinces have a large number of price reduction scenic spots, of which the number of price reduction scenic spots in Yunnan is more than 100, and the overall decline is more than 30%.
Anhui, Chongqing and other eight provinces (autonomous regions, municipalities) government pricing 5A-level scenic spots have all achieved a price reduction.
With high social attention, Yunnan Shilin, Dali Three Towers, Yulong Snow Mountain, Guangxi Guilin Lijiang, Fujian Wuyi Mountain, Hunan Zhangjiajie, Shaanxi soldiers, Jiangxi Sanqing Mountain, Xinjiang Kanas and other scenic spots have implemented price cuts.
Ticket prices in key state-owned scenic spots have gradually returned to a reasonable range, which is conducive to accelerating the transformation and upgrading of tourism from the ticket economy to the industrial economy, minority tourism to mass tourism, and tourism to global tourism, which is conducive to the formation of a virtuous circle of the optimization of the supply structure of tourism and the steady expansion of tourism consumption demand, and to promote the sustainable and healthy development of scenic spots and tourism.
At the same time, the National Development and Reform Commission stressed that all localities should strengthen the price order norms of scenic spots, guide scenic spots to improve services, and ensure that prices are not reduced.
In addition, on the problems such as the decline in ticket prices of individual scenic spots reflected by the media in the near future, the National Development and Reform Commission has carried out special inspections, requiring all localities to deal with them seriously, respond to social concerns in a timely manner, and effectively implement the price reduction in place.
The CCPIT has carried out short-, medium- and long-term optimization work in an orderly manner
The Macao Trade and Investment Promotion Bureau has submitted a report on the short-, medium and long-term optimization of "major investment immigration" and "skilled immigrants", and at present, in addition to stepping up the promotion and implementation of the work within the report, it has also continued to listen to the opinions of the community and continuously optimize the content of the report and related work.
As soon as possible, the CCPIT will introduce relevant optimization work to all sectors of society.
Among them, five are short-term measures that will be carried out during this year; five are medium-term measures to be carried out in 2019; and 1 is long-term measures.
In addition, the CCPIT also comprehensively reviewed the internal management system in accordance with the instructions of the Director of the Economic and Financial Affairs Department.
Five short-term measures carried out this year include:
To carry out to carry out the review work, give priority to the review of cases that are about to expire for seven years, the cases mentioned in the CCAC's report, and newly renewed cases. If cases of misconduct or signs of illegality are found, they will take the initiative to refer them to the relevant judicial organs for follow-up and treatment;
On-site inspections of projects involving “major investment immigrants” have been inspected by more than 20 investment projects by the end of September;
A comprehensive review of the current review system has been carried out. Six principles for analyzing investment projects have been re-established in reviewing applications for "major investment immigrants", and in reviewing "skilled immigrants" applications, the relevant approval mechanism will be improved by clarifying the elements conducive to the development of Macao and the conditions for preferentially absorbing talents. At the same time, a list of "five industries and ten types of jobs" for the introduction of talents has been established in an annual priority, so as to cooperate with the policy direction of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.
Continue to increase the transparency of information, including plans to gradually publish the approval standards, scoring standards and proportion from the fourth quarter of this year, and to further refine and disclose the approval data;
In terms of improving the work of the recognition mechanism, it has been required to check the working situation in Australia; major investments must go to the site to check and submit financial statements.
The five medium-term measures carried out in 2019 include:
To establish a mechanism for regularly listening to the views of the Talent Development Committee and the Economic Development Committee, which has held a working meeting with the Economic Development Committee in September to discuss the establishment of relevant mechanisms.
The applicant is required to submit annual financial statements made by an independent third party in order to continuously review the operation status of investment projects;
Further standardization and electronicization of individual application and approval processes to reduce anthropogenic errors;
A comprehensive review of the current manpower configuration, in line with the implementation of a number of optimization measures;
Stepping up the revision of the study of the temporary residence system for investors, managers and specially qualified technicians.
As for long-term measures to intensify the study of the revision of the law, it is expected that in the first half of 2019, the drafting of relevant laws and regulations will be carried out as soon as possible to further clarify the approval criteria, review mechanism and confirmation mechanism for temporary residence permits, and increase the investigation function of the CCPIT in order to more accurately approve and supervise applications for temporary residence permits.
The experts of the national filmless cotton on-site observation and discussion and exchange activities walked into the experimental field and listened to the presentation of the representatives of the academician team of the Chinese Academy of Engineering.
Xinzhong Xinjiang Shaya September 30th (Geng Dandan Wang Xiaojun) is located in Shaya County, Xinjiang filmless cotton planting test base, filmless cotton growth is happy, compared with the surrounding membrane cotton "not inferior", a cluster of snow-white cotton competing "open", hanging full of branches.
From September 27th to 28th, the national filmless cotton on-site observation and discussion and exchange activities were held in Shaya County, Xinjiang.
The reporter learned at the observation meeting that the membraneless cotton technology system with "China Cotton 619" and its supporting cultivation measures as the main body has initially achieved the goal of filmless cultivation of cotton fields, reducing the pollution of the ecological environment and raw cotton in the residual film of cotton fields in Xinjiang, and significant progress has been made in the comprehensive technical research and demonstration.
Academician of the Chinese Academy of Engineering, famous cotton genetic breeder and chief scientist of the cotton system of the national modern agricultural industry technology system Yu Shuxun introduced the growth situation of filmless cotton to Zhou Guomao, party secretary of Zhejiang University of Agriculture and Forestry.
"The comprehensive technology we have developed for filmless cotton can completely realize the cultivation of cotton without film, which can completely solve the problem of residual film pollution and achieve green cotton planting."
Academician of the Chinese Academy of Engineering Yu Shuxun was introduced.
According to the statistics of the National Bureau of Statistics, Xinjiang's cotton planting area in 2017 was 35 million mu, accounting for 61% of the country's cotton area.
Since the introduction of land film into China in 1982, all kinds of crops in Xinjiang have covered more than 50 million mu, and the annual use of land membranes is about 300,000 tons.
Among them, the coverage rate of cotton film has reached 100%, and cotton laminating accounts for about 60% of Xinjiang's membrane use.
Membrane-free cotton is measured, and cotton production can fully achieve a yield of 320 kg to 350 kg per mu.
With the continuous increase of land film input in Xinjiang, the recovery rate of the residual film is low, the amount of residual film in the soil has gradually increased, and a series of problems such as soil structure damage caused by the residual film have seriously affected the sustainable development of agriculture.
The residual film not only causes serious pollution to the soil, but also has a great impact on the quality of cotton fibers.
At present, more than one-third of the cotton fields in Xinjiang have achieved mechanized harvesting.
In 2017, Xinjiang's organic cotton mining area was about 14 million mu.
In the process of cotton harvesting, it is difficult to remove the crushed film on a large number of surface and cotton plants, and it is difficult to remove the crushed film doped in the raw cotton processing process, and it cannot be completely removed during subsequent textile processing, which seriously affects the quality of textile products.
On September 28, the national filmless cotton on-site observation and discussion and exchange activities were held in Shaya County, Xinjiang.
In order to focus on solving the pollution of cotton fields, simplifying cotton planting technology, and improving the efficiency of cotton fields, Yu Shuxun led his team through 8 years, the implementation of "cotton 619" filmless cotton technology planting, for the green development of Xinjiang's agriculture "wing".
Through the new ideas of innovative breeding, we will cultivate a new type of land-based cotton 619 that is precocious, saline-resistant, low-temperature-resistant and abundant.
â€œChinese cotton 619â€ in the southern part of Xinjiang without membrane cultivation conditions, to achieve film-free sowing machinery supporting, sowing depth improvement, non-membrane conditions of dripping pipe shallow burial, suitable sowing density screening, reasonable chemical control and a series of supporting measures."
At present, Aksu, Kurle, Aral and other places have established filmless cotton demonstration bases, with a yield of 4,800 kilograms per hectare.
The cultivation of cotton without film has achieved abundant production, cost savings, environmental protection, and improved comprehensive benefits.
Zhang Donghai, an agronomist in the third division of the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps, said that through nearly 6 years of filmless cotton cultivation technology research and demonstration, the yield of filmless cotton cotton can fully achieve a yield of 320 kilograms to 350 kilograms per mu, and may even be higher.
â€œThere is a great prospect for the promotion of filmless cotton cultivation technology.â€
Zhang Donghai believes that at present, membraneless cotton cultivation technology can completely solve the problem of soil residual film pollution, but there is still a certain gap in economic benefits compared to membrane cultivation.
â€œThe support of the purchase price of cotton will be conducive to the promotion in the future.â€
In the next step, he and his team will continue to conduct in-depth research and large-scale promotion and application of filmless cotton, make the filmless cotton industry bigger and stronger, and completely solve the problem of soil pollution caused by the membrane.
Guangdang sea, land and air to actively respond to the National Day Golden Week transport - Sino-Singapore network
September 29 is the seventh day of the official opening of the Hong Kong section of the high-speed rail, and it is also the first weekend after the opening, and the head of the West Kowloon Station.
The National Day Golden Week (October 1 to 7) holiday is approaching, in recent days, the reporter learned from the relevant departments, Guangdong railways, aviation, water transport, roads and other transportation departments actively planning, increase capacity delivery, the introduction of various safeguard measures to ensure that domestic passenger transportation is safe and orderly.
China Railway Guangzhou Bureau Group Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as "Guangzhou Railway Group") said that during this year's National Day Golden Week, Guangzhou Railway Group is expected to transport 17.8 million passengers, an increase of 1.505 million passengers, an increase of 9.2%.
In order to meet the travel needs of passengers, Canton Railway Group plans to open 104 high-speed trains and 85 high-speed trains, which are mainly concentrated in popular lines such as Beijing-Guangzhou, Shanghai-Kun, Guangzhou-Shenzhen-Hong Kong, and Hangzhou-Shenzhen-Shenzhen-high-speed rail.
Guangzhou Baiyun Airport may become the busiest airport in the mainland during the National Day Golden Week this year, and it is expected to transfer more than 1.4 million passengers and more than 9,200 flights.
With the increasing number of international routes, the airport is expected to increase significantly compared with the past, and the substantial increase in international passengers will be a significant feature of this year's Golden Week holiday.
It is understood that Singapore, Bangkok, Phuket, Jakarta, Colombo, the Maldives, Manila and other places are this year's National Day holiday travel hot cities, Kathmandu, Kuala Lumpur, Bali and other popular tourist destinations also continue to hot, part of the flight "a ticket is difficult to find".
Some airlines have especially increased their operations, such as: Shenzhen Airlines added one new Guangzhou-Hanoi flights per day; Iran's Mahan Airlines added 1 new Guangzhou-Tehran flight every Saturday; Vietnam Airlines added one new Guangzhou-Hanoi flights every Tuesday and Thursday.
In order to do a good job in holiday protection, Baiyun Airport has increased key post guarantees such as â€œstation allocationâ€, â€œbaggage guaranteeâ€ , â€œcheck-in servicesâ€ , â€œpassenger security inspectionâ€ , etc., and is ready for large-scale delays on flights.
China Southern Airlines said that this year's National Day Golden Week to Australia and New Zealand, North America and Japan and South Korea routes are very hot, and flights to Hainan, Chengdu, Luzhou, Jiuhua Mountain, Anshan, Huangshan and other mainland Chinese tourism destinations are also relatively tight.
China Southern plans to add 50 flights during Golden Week, including 10 flights between Guangzhou and Chiang Mai.
According to the Guangdong Maritime Bureau, before the festival, key ships such as water sightseeing tourist ships, Qiongzhou Strait passenger ferries, Zhujiangkou high-speed passenger ships, and ferry crossings have carried out safety hazard investigation actions to ensure that the water traffic safety situation is stable during the long holiday period.
During the Golden Week, the traffic flow in Guangdong Province is expected to rank first in China.
The Guangdong Provincial Transportation Group recently issued guidelines for holiday highway travel, which is expected to increase by about 12%.
The General Administration of Market Supervision recently issued a notice on strengthening the supervision of market prices during the 2018 Mid-Autumn National Day, which requires strengthening price supervision in the field of housing leasing and real estate, severely rectifying price collusion, hoarding rental sources, fabricating false information to raise rents, charging fees in the form of bundled services, publishing misleading price information, and unspecified price violations.
The notice is clear, it is necessary to strengthen the price monitoring warning and pay close attention to market price dynamics.
All localities should pay close attention to daily necessities such as large-consumption grain, oil, poultry, egg and vegetable milk salt, as well as the market and price changes of local residents' holiday consumption of specialty commodities, and strengthen price monitoring and analysis of early warnings.
Once it is found that the market is prone to fluctuation and early problems, timely measures should be taken to resolve them effectively.
It is necessary to strengthen the supervision and inspection of the wholesale and retail links of daily necessities, increase the monitoring frequency and supervision of places closely related to the daily consumption of the masses, and urge operators to abide by the law and operate in good faith.
The notice pointed out that it is necessary to strengthen the inspection of key areas and create a good holiday consumption environment; strengthen the supervision of ticket prices in state-owned scenic spots; focus on investigating and punishing state-owned scenic spots not to implement the price level or floating range stipulated by the government, adding additional charging items without authorization, increasing ticket prices in the forms such as illegally setting "Garden Park" tickets, high pricing discounts, bundled sales, not according to the provisions of preferential measures.
The notice requires strengthening the supervision of the prices of daily necessities, especially agricultural products.
Affected by seasonal changes, natural disasters and sudden epidemics, the prices of vegetables, pork and other essential agricultural products in some areas have fluctuated recently.
All localities should combine local actual conditions to effectively strengthen the market price supervision of agricultural by-products, cooperate with relevant departments to stabilize production and market supply work, and organize forces to carry out key market inspections and random spot checks.
For commodities such as pork with tight supply and faster price increases, the frequency of inspections will be increased, and illegal acts such as hoarding, raising prices, and collusively rising prices have been seriously investigated.
The notice pointed out that it is necessary to strengthen price supervision in the field of housing leasing and real estate.
Mid-Autumn and National Day coincides with the peak season of housing rental and commercial housing sales, all localities should pay close attention to the price behavior of real estate enterprises, intermediary companies and housing rental-related enterprises, strictly rectify rent prices collusion, hoard rental sources, fabricate false information to raise rents, charge fees in the form of bundling services, publish misleading price information, unspecified price labeling and other price violations, and increase the inspection of the real estate market.
The notice mentioned that all localities should effectively do a good job in price supervision in other aspects of the tourism industry, focus on standardizing the price order of catering, accommodation, shopping, sightseeing, entertainment, parking and other links, guide operators to do a good job of marking prices and charging publicity, and seriously investigate and deal with all kinds of price violations.
The notice said that it is necessary to strengthen the inspection of transportation prices such as highways, railways, civil aviation, and water transportation, and seriously investigate and deal with violations such as illegal price increases, out-of-price charges, and not in accordance with the regulations.
Implement the "green channel" for the transportation of live agricultural products and the policy of exempting small bus tolls on major holidays.
It is necessary to innovate regulatory means and working methods, strengthen the publicity of price laws and regulations of online and offline commodity retail enterprises and e-commerce platforms, urge operators to improve price promotion plans, and investigate and deal with fictitious original prices, misleading price labels, non-fulfilment of price commitments and other illegal acts in accordance with the law.
The reporter learned on the 1st that on the 15th anniversary of the Shanghai-Hong Kong train, it has experienced three accelerations, and so far the passenger flow has continued to grow; the total number of passengers carrying to and from Shanghai and Hong Kong has exceeded 1.7 million.
At the same time, Hong Kong and Macao passengers passed the clearance for no more than 15 seconds.
On October 1, 2003, the State Council approved the establishment of a temporary port for Shanghai-Jiulong straight-through trains, and the Shanghai railway port, as the first long-distance long-distance railway passenger port in China, marks that Shanghai has an opening pattern of ports with water, aviation, and land routes.
So far, the Shanghai-Hong Kong train has been in direct operation for 15 years.
Shanghai railway border inspection, which is responsible for the task of entering and exiting from Shanghai and Hong Kong, disclosed on the 1st that since it was opened, Shanghai-Hong Kong trains have been speeded up three times, and the one-way travel time has been shortened from nearly 30 hours to 19 hours; the average annual passenger travestion of inbound and outbound passengers has increased from less than 80,000 to more than 150,000; in the past 15 years, the total number of passengers transported to and from Shanghai and Hong Kong has exceeded 1.7 million.
It is reported that in the past 15 years, the Shanghai Railway Entry-Exit Border Checkpoint and the Shanghai-Jiu train stations along the way signed a police coordination mechanism, and sent police officers to carry out car supervision, to achieve 1991 km of service and control full coverage.
In the past 15 years, nearly 1,000 cases of all kinds of violations have been seized at the border inspection station of the Shanghai Railway, which have successfully cracked the cases of foreigners smuggling out of the country with false certificates, and the cases of impersonation with other people's documents.
The station has also established working exchanges and other mechanisms with joint inspection units, regularly carried out comprehensive counter-terrorism drills at railway ports, coordinated defense linkage, and built a "three-level moat" protective belt at railway ports.
It is understood that in the past 15 years, the border inspection department of the Shanghai railway has continuously innovated its services, and the customs clearance speed has been greatly improved.
The border inspection station also set up a "Jinglan" volunteer service group to provide caring assistance for the elderly, pregnant women and passengers with babies.
The reporter learned from the Ministry of Finance on the 30th that the four departments of the Ministry of Finance, the State Administration of Taxation, the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce recently jointly issued a notice to further encourage foreign investors to invest in China and the profits distributed by foreign investors from domestic resident enterprises in China, and to use domestic direct investment not to collect the scope of application of income tax policies, and to expand by foreign investment encouragement projects to all non-prohibited foreign investment projects and areas.
This policy has been implemented since January 1, 2018.
The notice made it clear that the direct investment made by foreign investors in terms of profits, including equity investment behaviors such as capital increases, new constructions, and equity acquisitions carried out by foreign investors by sharing profits, does not include the addition, conversion or acquisition of shares of listed companies in addition to eligible strategic investments.
Foreign investors in accordance with the provisions can enjoy the temporary non-levigated income tax policy, but not actually enjoyed, you can actually pay the relevant taxes within three years from the date of apply for recovery to enjoy the policy, the return of paid taxes.
Not only that, after foreign investors enjoy the provisions of the provisions of the temporary collection of advance income tax policy treatment, the investment enterprise reorganization meets the conditions of special reorganization, and in practice in accordance with the special reorganization for tax processing, you can continue to enjoy the temporary collection of advance income tax policy treatment.
In order to ensure that the profits received by foreign investors are actually used for direct investment, the notice stipulates that the profits used by foreign investors for direct investment are paid in cash, the relevant funds are directly transferred from the account of the profit-distributing enterprise to the account of the invested enterprise or the equity transferor, and may not be turned around in other accounts at home and abroad before direct investment; the profits used by foreign investors for direct investment are paid in the form of non-cash, and the ownership of the relevant assets is transferred directly from the profit-distributing enterprise to the invested enterprise or equity transfer.
The notice also requires the tax department to strengthen follow-up management in accordance with the law.
Foreign investors have enjoyed the temporary non-collection of advance income tax policy, after the follow-up management of the tax department to verify that does not meet the prescribed conditions, in addition to belonging to the profit distribution of corporate responsibility, is regarded as foreign investors in accordance with the provisions of the declaration of corporate income tax, will be investigated in accordance with the law to delay the payment of tax liability, tax deferred payment period calculated from the date of payment of related profits.
The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) said on Friday it would no longer allow imports of raw materials made by China's Huahai Pharmaceuticals and those made from the company's APIs.
A drug previously produced by Huahai Pharmaceutical has been recalled because it contains potentially carcinogenic substances.
The European Medicines Agency said it was considering further action on other ingredients produced by the plant.
According to the FDA, major production process problems were found when the FDA inspected Huahai Pharmaceutical's pharmaceutical companies, and then stopped imports.
The FDA also said that it will be banned from imports until Huahai Pharmaceutical finds how these impurities are generated and improves its quality control system.
Huahai Pharmaceutical issued a statement on the company's website on September 29, saying: "For the problems in the official inspection of the United States and Europe, the company is undergoing rectification with a positive attitude and strong measures; for the official treatment of the United States and Europe and the results, the company is very surprised and regrettable.
In the current complex market environment, the company is worried about this.
At present, the company is organizing teams, including professional lawyers, in accordance with the relevant procedures and the United States and EU officials to communicate and lodge complaints, in order to resume production as soon as possible.
SHANGHAI, Sept 29 (Reuters) - The China Securities Regulatory Commission announced late on Friday that the SFC approved the initial application (IPO) of People's Insurance Group Co., Ltd. in accordance with legal procedures.
However, the SFC's official WeChat public account did not disclose the scale of this IPO fundraising.
As early as September 29 last year, the China Insurance (1339.HK) applied to the China Securities Regulatory Commission to issue up to 4.599 billion A shares, which is planned to be listed on the Shanghai Stock Exchange.
According to the pre-disclosure materials previously published by the SFC, the number of new shares the company's application does not exceed 9.78% of the total share capital issued after listing, and does not include any shares that may be issued according to the over-allocation option.
The raised funds will be used to enrich the company's capital.
On April 9 this year, the CSRC announced the prospectus (declaration draft) guaranteed by China.
According to the prospectus, before the issuance of A shares, the total share capital of China's insurance was 42.424 billion shares, assuming that 4.599 billion shares of A shares were issued and the over-allotment option was not exercised, and after the A-shares were issued, the group's total equity did not exceed 47.023 billion shares, of which A shares did not exceed 38.296 billion shares, and the number of H shares was 8.726 billion shares.
On June 5, the Chinese insurance IPO application passed the press conference.
As of December 31, 2017, the Ministry of Finance held 70.47 percent of China's total share capital and 10.2 percent from the Social Security Foundation.
After the People's Republic of China guarantees the issuance of shares in A shares, the shareholding ratio of the Ministry of Finance will be diluted to 63.58%, and the shareholding ratio of the Social Security Foundation will be 9.2%.
As of Friday, China's guaranteed H shares closed at HK$3.52, up 1.44% on the same day.
Former foreign aid accuses of playing counterfeiting Northern control response "unwarranted"-Zhongxin.com
Yesterday afternoon, Beijing Holding Football Club (hereinafter referred to as North Control) in response to the team's former foreign aid Anichebe accused the team of allegedly kicking the fake ball of the news of the official response, the northern control side issued a statement that there is absolutely no situation in the club's side to kick the fake ball, which is exactly Anichebe himself in the arbitration process, in order to cover up his flagrant violation of the fact of the contract, for his personal improper economic purposes out of thin air to create lies.
At the same time, Northern Control said that it will reserve the right to hold all relevant parties accountable by all means.
According to the British "Daily Mail" news, Nigerian player Anichebe accused FIFA that he had played last year's Beijing control team was suspected of playing counterfeiting, including the Beijing derby in the 21st round of A in the 2017 season.
At that time, it was the key stage of Beijing people and punching, and the North control of the game finally lost 0 to 2 to the Beijingers and Anicheby.
For the Nigerian player's statement, yesterday's official response from the northern control club.
According to the statement, after a previous internal investigation by the club, there was no situation in which the team participated in the game.
Anichebe joined Beijing North Control in June 2017, and in December of the same year, Anichebe refused to return to the team to participate in winter training without justifiable reasons, and still refused to return to the team under the circumstances of the club's repeated complaints.
At present, the dispute between the two parties has been submitted to FIFA, and the arbitration is ongoing.
The statement also mentioned that the high-profile "counterfeiting accusation" is actually a lie fabricated out of thin air for his personal improper economic purposes in order to cover up the fact of his blatant breach of contractual agreements during the arbitration process.
The sole purpose of defaming clubs and slandering Chinese football is to obtain improper economic benefits.
The club also does not accept any organization or any individual who, for the sake of its financial interests and personal grievances, engages in unwarranted accusations, slanders, slanders and denigrations against the club.
Therefore, the northern control side said that it will reserve the right to hold all relevant parties accountable by all means.
The Agricultural Development Bank of China will invest 20 billion yuan to support the acquisition of Jilin autumn grain.
Since September, crops from all over Jilin Province have ushered in the peak harvest period.
The reporter learned from the branch of Jilin Province of the Agricultural Development Bank of China that at present, the agricultural issuance has provided enough 20 billion yuan of credit funds to ensure that Jilin autumn grain acquisition funds are sufficient.
It is understood that the food production situation in Jilin is generally stable this year, and some grain processing enterprises have increased food market demand due to the expansion of production capacity and the increase in operating rates.
In order to ensure the supply of funds for grain policy acquisitions, agricultural issuance has actively carried out autumn grain acquisition of bank enterprises through visits to farmers, processing enterprises, trading enterprises and other acquisition entities.
At present, agricultural issuance has invested 5.2 billion yuan to support all kinds of grain acquisition subjects to acquire 11.58 billion pounds of autumn grain.
There have been 120 major grain acquisition subjects in Jilin Province layout of nearly 300 acquisition outlets, to ensure that the main grain producing counties "full coverage", do not leave the acquisition of capital supply "blank point".
The relevant person in charge of agricultural issuance said that according to the progress of the acquisition and the demand for enterprise funds, if there is a shortage of acquisition funds, the agricultural issuance will apply for an increase on the basis of 20 billion yuan of credit funds to ensure the timely and full supply of funds, maintain the stability of the grain market, and protect the interests of farmers.
Chinese journalists will be taken away by the police in the British Conservative Party year, and the Chinese side demands an apology.
According to the website of the Chinese Embassy in the United Kingdom, the spokesman of the British Embassy responded to questions from reporters on the 1st when a Chinese journalist was taken away by the police during the annual meeting of the British Conservative Party.
"We demand that the Conservative Human Rights Commission stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop meddling in Hong Kong affairs, and ask the organizers of the meeting to apologize to Chinese journalists."
Q: During the annual meeting of the British Conservative Party on September 30, the party's Human Rights Commission held a side meeting on the Hong Kong issue and invited the Hong Kong opposition to speak.
A Chinese journalist was taken away by the police during the meeting.
Please, do you have any comments?
In response, the spokesperson said that in the past 21 years since Hong Kong's return to the motherland, the practice of "one country, two systems" has achieved great success, and Hong Kong's development achievements have been universally recognized.
Hong Kong is China's Hong Kong, and Hong Kong affairs are purely China's internal affairs.
The Conservative Human Rights Commission has used the party's annual meeting to hold a side event for anti-China separatist forces, and China expresses its grave concern and strong dissatisfaction.
We are firmly opposed to any interference by any organization in Hong Kong's affairs in any way
Any attempt to promote “Hong Kong’s independence” is futile.
The spokesman said that the United Kingdom has always advertised freedom of speech, but when Chinese journalists asked questions and expressed their views at the sidelines, they were blocked and even physically violated, which was completely unacceptable.
We call on the Conservative Human Rights Commission to stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop meddling in Hong Kong affairs, and ask the conference organizers to apologize to Chinese journalists.
The 5th World Internet Conference will be held in Wuzhen, Zhejiang from November 7th to 9th, and the World Internet is about to enter "Wuzhen Time" again.
As a global Internet industry event, the World Internet Conference has received great attention and wide recognition in the global Internet field.
In the past five years, the World Internet Conference has built a big stage for Internet cutting-edge technology display and exchange, and the wide application of technical achievements at the conference has added new impetus to global economic development.
The release of the results brings together the world's Internet cutting-edge science and technology
In the field of the Internet, what are the top and most striking achievements in the world today?
The leading scientific and technological achievements released by the World Internet Conference can give answers.
For the first time, the 3rd World Internet Conference released 15 leading scientific and technological achievements.
The results shown are active in innovation, wide range of applications, and the driving role of radiation, reflecting the latest and most important scientific and technological breakthroughs in the field of the global Internet at that time, reflecting the speed and future prospects for the development of the online information field.
Optical quantum computers, 5G, artificial intelligence capable of calculating emotions, etc. The results released by the 4th World Internet Conference are even more dazzling.
The organizing committee of the conference set up a recommendation committee for the world's Internet leading scientific and technological achievements, composed of 44 well-known experts and scholars from 10 countries such as China and the United States, collecting nearly 1,000 innovative achievements in the Internet field from all countries in the world, and finally evaluated 18 representative achievements, including "Huawei 3GPP 5G pre-commercial system", "Arm security architecture", "Microsoft Little Ice", "Beidou satellite navigation system" and "based on the major application results of Shenwei and Taihu' supercomputer system".
At present, the application of "Beidou satellite navigation system" covers more than 50 countries and regions, involving more than 3 billion people.
The Shenwei Taihu Light supercomputer has completed more than 2 million operational tasks and supported the research of more than 100 applications.
Starting from China pioneered by Microsoft's Chinese R&D team, "Microsoft Little Ice" has now landed in China, Japan, the United States, India, Indonesia and other countries, serving as television presenters, radio hosts, singers and many other roles. The development of China's Internet science and technology has frequently flashed into the world's scientific and technological cutting-edge camp, attracting the world's surprised attention and becoming the world's top Internet science and technology.
"The Light of the Internet" Expo Builds a New Platform for Technical Exchanges
As one of the important contents of the World Internet Conference, the "Light of the Internet" Expo drives the interactive exchange of the achievements of global Internet scientific and technological innovation, and builds an important platform for Internet companies to show their latest achievements.
"Internet Light" Expo shows the new achievements, new technologies and new applications of the Internet around the world, with different thematic exhibition areas and functional plates, according to different scientific and technological classifications, selecting the world's well-known Internet companies and innovative enterprises, gathering cutting-edge achievements, showing innovative technologies, reflecting the light of civilization, the light of the future and the light of the world.
Taking the 4th World Internet Conference "Light of the Internet" Expo as an example, the expo attracted 411 well-known domestic and foreign enterprises from all over the world to participate in the exhibition, and the latest achievements of global Internet technology and application innovation and digital economic development such as cloud computing, Internet of Things, and artificial intelligence highlighted the characteristics of global vision, innovation-driven and open cooperation.
More than 110 new product and new technology release activities held during the conference, and 10 Internet project cooperation special matchmaking meetings, providing a broad stage for global digital economy cooperation.
A paper test paper, scanned by mobile phones or tablets, can immediately identify the content and approve the score; half a meter high driverless small car with goods, which can independently complete fast delivery; only with the owner's voice instructions, the smart home can achieve voice shopping, mobile phone recharge, take-out, music playback, "Internet Light" exposition of a top Internet science and technology achievements, has become the global science and technology industry and the Internet development of the wind vane, built a new platform.
The development results of Internet science and technology for the benefit of all peoples
The innovation and development driven by Internet technology is ultimately to create a better future for the peoples of the world, and to create a more equal, open and inclusive environment for the happiness of mankind, economic development and the beauty of society.
In China, an Internet country with a huge user base, Internet technology has a strong amplification effect in specific applications.
For example, China Beidou provides users with high-precision, high-reliability positioning, speed measurement and timing services, and has unique short message communication capabilities; the rapid development of artificial intelligence technology has remodeling functions for traditional industries, promoting industry progress, and playing a positive role in many fields such as finance, transportation, health, and safety; communication technology helps to effectively solve the online problems of vehicles such as aircraft and high-speed rail, and improves the user's online experience.
According to the 42nd "Statistical Report on the Development of China's Internet Network" released by the China Internet Network Information Center, as the world's largest Internet market, China is promoting social development and progress with the digital process.
The dividend of Internet technology development is not limited to China, and its achievements have also brought strong impetus to the development of the Internet in the whole world and even the development of economy and society.
For example, China's cross-border e-commerce and sharing economy have gone overseas, supporting the world's economic growth; China's new generation of information technology such as cloud computing, big data, the Internet of Things, and the mobile Internet has accelerated the deepening of the global industrial division of labor and economic restructuring, and reshaped the global economic competition pattern.
As outlined in the "Wuzhen Initiative" released by the Second World Internet Conference, sharing the achievements of network development, promoting the early formation of a global online market and creating more employment opportunities, will provide strong support for the sustained and healthy development of the global economy, so that more countries and people can take the express train of the information age.
Lu Liang is known as the "Kingdom of miscellaneous grains".
From September 30th to October 7th, the 2nd Lüliang famous excellent functional food exhibition and the first farmers harvest festival were held in Shanxi Luliang Fenyang City.
During the event, representatives of officials from Lüliang's Shizhi District, Fenyang City, Jiaocheng County, Lan County and other places invited tourists to experience the beauty of the countryside through on-site promotion and jointly celebrate the farmers' harvest festival.
On the eve of the National Day, it is the autumn harvest season, known as the "Kingdom of miscellaneous grains" Lvliang held a "host grain event", and more than 200 merchants participated in 426 kinds of well-known functional foods to participate in the exhibition and sales.
As one of the main production areas in Shanxi, Lan County in recent years through the research and development of potato practices, extending the industrial chain, in the development of the industry at the same time to drive the villagers out of poverty, the scene, exhibitors through the "potato feast" dishes display, introduced the new way of eating potatoes; merchants from Lin County brought fresh dates, green beans, peas, millet and so on.
Luliang agriculture has a long history, grain cultivation began in the Neolithic era, soybeans, beans, porcupines, glutinous seeds, etc. There is a history of cultivation of four or five thousand years, and red jujube planting can be traced back to the Western Han Dynasty.
The unique climate and diverse landscape have formed many special agricultural products in Luliang, and it is a well-known national production base of red dates, walnuts, miscellaneous grains and fragrant white wine.
At present, Lüliang City has initially formed special production bases such as Linxian County, Liulin red dates, Fenyang, Zhongyang walnuts, Lan County Potatoes, Xingxian small miscellaneous grains, Fangshan herbal medicine, edible fungi, filial piety facilities and vegetables, Wenshui sand buckthorns, stone tower honey and other specialty production base counties, which have certified pollution-free green organic products with an area of 1.6 million mu and 172 products.
More than 200 merchants participated in the exhibition with 426 kinds of special functional foods.
Li Zhengyin, vice chairman of the Political Consultative Conference of Shanxi Province and secretary of the Luliang Municipal Party Committee, said that the city will further expand the opening up of agriculture, promote the docking of production and marketing, and promote Luliang's more well-known functional foods to the whole country and to the world.
In addition to picking pastoral melons and fruits, the beauty of the countryside is also in the ecological countryside to enjoy the actual performances.
During the event, representatives of officials from Stone District, Fenyang City, Jiaocheng County, Lan County and other places introduced local scenic spots to the participants and invited tourists to visit.
Li Huiyi, deputy mayor of Fenyang City, introduced that there are Song Dynasty Yusheng General Diqing in Fenyang, and now there is a well-known director Jia Zhangke; in addition to the folk culture such as the popular Fenzhou Dijing song, "no fence is not a drama", there are tourist attractions "Chinese wine almond blossom village, rural revitalization of Jiajiazhuang, ecological sacred ancient lake.
The implementation of the rural revitalization strategy and the promotion of agricultural supply-side reform are the means of poverty alleviation for Lüliang as a special hardship area.
Li Zhengyin admitted that to win the battle against poverty, consumer poverty alleviation is a very important way to enable the people in poor areas to achieve poverty alleviation and increase income, "we warmly hope that friends from all walks of life 'buy products in poor areas, dedication to poverty alleviation and love'."
With the theme of "celebrating the harvest, promoting culture, and revitalizing the countryside", the event aims to invite tourists to â€œPractical characteristics of mountain treasures, appreciation of folklore culture, beautiful scenery â€œLiuliangâ€ , â€œLiu Liang walnuts â€œLiuliang walnutsâ€ , â€œLuliang miscellaneous foodsâ€ and other well-known agricultural products with a high reputation and market competitiveness.
During the event, there will also be investment attraction and trade signing activities, as well as awards activities such as "the top ten planting masters", "the top ten rich leaders", "the top ten rural e-commerce leaders" and "the top ten famous chefs".
Xiamen Municipal People's Government recently issued a notice, since October 1st, migrant workers holding Xiamen city residence permit for 5 consecutive years, in Xiamen City to go through the employment registration formalities and participate in the social pension insurance for 5 consecutive years and in Xiamen to own the "Xiamen land and housing rights certificate" real estate, can move the hukou into.
Residents who have completed the 5th anniversary in Jimei District, Haicang District, Tong'an District or Xiang'an District and have completed the 5th anniversary of employment registration in Xiamen City and participated in Xiamen's social old-age insurance for the fifth consecutive anniversary, and have the "Xiamen City Land Housing Certificate" real estate in Siming District and Huli District.
At present, there are six municipal districts in Xiamen City, which are divided into Siming District and Huli District on the island; Haicang District, Jimei District, Tong'an District and Xiang'an District outside the island.
This is the first time since August 2010 that Xiamen has relaxed the conditions for settling in Xiamen Island.
Xinhua News Agency, Fuzhou, October 1 (Reporter Xiu Xiao'an) On October 1, the "Fujian Province high-speed railway safety management regulations" was officially implemented.
The regulations put forward that within 500 meters on each side of the high-speed rail power line wire, it is forbidden to fly kites, balloons, pore lights, aircraft and other airborne objects and small aircraft.
On the basis of superior laws such as the Railway Law of the People's Republic of China and the Regulations on Railway Safety Management, according to the geographical and climatic characteristics of Fujian Province, supplementary provisions are made on prohibited and restricted acts affecting the safety of high-speed rail, standardizing acts such as high-speed rail construction and tree planting, further clarifying the main body and scope of supervision of high-speed rail supervision, and clarifying law enforcement supervision responsibilities and legal responsibilities.
The provisions for Fujian Province coastal wind, high-speed rail along the light construction materials and light floating materials are blown into the high-speed rail to affect the safety of the situation, the provisions of the high-speed rail power lines on both sides of the range of 500 meters, prohibit the release of kites, balloons, pore lights, power umbrellas, aircraft and other airborne objects and small aircraft.
In addition, plastic greenhouses, colored steel plates, sunshades and other lightweight objects along the high-speed rail, as well as low-altitude floating objects, plastic protective films and other light objects generated during the construction process, everyone or users should take strengthening protective measures to prevent the safety of high-speed rail.
In view of the many characteristics of Fujian Province's hilly areas and high-speed railway tunnels, it is stipulated that within 200 meters of the central line above the high-speed rail tunnel, the construction of mountain ponds, reservoirs, levees, the excavation of river channels, dry canals, wells and other behaviors that may affect the safety of the tunnel should be solicited from railway construction units or railway transportation enterprises.
At the same time, those who violate the relevant responsibilities of the Provisions will be ordered by the public security organ to make corrections; if the circumstances are more serious, the unit shall be fined not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan, and a fine of not less than 200 yuan but not more than 500 yuan for individuals; if the circumstances are serious, the unit shall be fined not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 30,000 yuan, and a fine of not more than 500 yuan but not more than 1,000 yuan for an individual.
If losses are caused, liability shall be borne in accordance with the law.
It is understood that with the rapid development of railway construction, Fujian Province's high-speed railway mileage of 200 kilometers per hour and above has now reached 1,516 kilometers, to realize the city's open train, it is expected that in the next five years, Fujian's domestic speed of 200 kilometers per hour and above railway lines will reach 2,150 kilometers.
The implementation of this provision will regulate the safety management of high-speed rail in Fujian Province, further implement the responsibilities of local government departments, coordinate railways and local forces, work together to ensure high-speed rail safety, and improve the high-speed rail safety prevention and control system in Fujian Province.
HONG KONG, Nov 5 (Reuters) - China's largest brewer, China's largest brewer, China's brewer (0291.HK), announced on Monday its acquisition of six breweries set up by Heineken/Hein.As in the mainland, as well as all of Hong Kong's issued share capital, at a total cost of about HK$2.355 billion.
At the same time, the company signed a trademark licensing association with Heene to authorize China Resources and Xue to manufacture, market, distribute and sell licensed products in mainland China, Hong Kong and Macao using the relevant Heineken® trademarks for a period of 20 years, followed by renewal in accordance with the same terms and conditions for a period of 10 years, until the termination clause of the trademark license agreement is terminated.
In August of this year, CR Beer announced that its direct controlling shareholder, China Resources Group (Beer) Co., Ltd., and Heili reached an equity cooperation agreement involving about HK$28.5 billion.
At the same time, China Resources Beer and Heineken reached a long-term strategic cooperation arrangement, which includes the acquisition of Heineken's existing businesses in China, Hong Kong and Macao, and the integration with CR Beer's beer business in China.
The transaction is the further implementation of this cooperation agreement.
China Resources Beer said that the transaction with Heineken provides the Group with an important strategy, long-term development and value enhancement opportunity to expand into the high-end beer market, so the long-term cooperative relationship established by the two sides will be highly complementary.
CR Beer closed at HK$28.85 on Friday, down nearly 4.5% over the past month.
Indonesia's strong earthquake after the tsunami devastated, the number of people killed or as many as thousands as thousands
According to comprehensive reports, a 7.5-magnitude shallow earthquake occurred on September 28 on the Indonesian island of Sulawesi, triggering a 6-meter-high tsunami.
According to the national disaster response department on September 30, the death toll increased to 832, mainly concentrated in Palu, the capital, and Dungala County, neighboring the epicenter of the earthquake.
Vice President Carla pointed out that because the number of casualties has not yet been calculated in some of the affected areas, the number of casualties may be as many as thousands.
A strong earthquake in Indonesia's Central Sulawesi province on the afternoon of September 28 and the resulting tsunami have killed 832 people.
2.4 million people affected by the collapse of thousands of buildings
Thousands of buildings have collapsed and several roads have broken, according to an estimated 2.4 million people.
Only 24 guests escaped safely after the collapse of a hotel on the local coast, and an estimated 50 to 60 people were trapped in rubble, with calls for help from time to time at the scene, and rescuers successfully rescued a young woman on September 30.
Due to ensuring the safety of the trapped people, the authorities were unable to use heavy machinery to remove the rubble, and the search and rescue progress was slow.
A shopping mall in the city also collapsed, and hundreds of residents rushed to the scene, waiting for news from relatives and friends.
Many residents use social platforms to send posts in search of separated relatives and friends.
On September 30, local time, a hotel collapsed and rescue work was carried out in the city of Central Sulawesi Balu, Indonesia.
10,000 people in Palu are waiting to be rescued, and the whereabouts of five foreigners are unknown.
Authorities said about 10,000 people in Palu were waiting for rescue and were scattered across 50 locations.
It is reported that 71 foreigners were in Palu at the time of the earthquake, of which 66 are temporarily known to be safe, including 21 Chinese citizens, the remaining 2 French people, two Malaysian tourists and 1 South Korean are unaccounted for.
The Chinese Embassy in Indonesia is using various channels to understand and verify the situation of Chinese citizens in the affected areas, and has not yet received reports of casualties among Chinese citizens.
Communications in Dongala County, adjacent to the epicentre of the earthquake, were still disrupted, and it was temporarily learned that 11 people were killed, but there was no more detailed information.
According to the scene, the coastal areas and ports of Dungara County were seriously damaged, a large number of buildings were swept away, the bodies were scattered everywhere, and Red Cross rescue teams were going to the local search and rescue.
Indonesia's president inspects the disaster, says reconstruction work to begin as soon as possible
The roads in Palu and Dongala were severely damaged, and only the aircraft carrying relief supplies were opened at Palu airport on September 30, allowing relief supplies and personnel to arrive as soon as soon as possible and transporting the seriously injured.
Many local hospitals are still without electricity, and the injured are receiving treatment outdoors.
More than 10,000 people were admitted to reception centers, and some feared that aftershocks would not dare to go home, preferring to spend the night outdoors.
Following the collapse of a prison in Palu, which caused hundreds of prisoners to escape, more than 100 prisoners in Dongala County also took advantage of the chaos caused by the earthquake, and prisoners set fire to the detention center.
Indonesian President Joko Widodo visited Palu on September 30 to inspect the disaster, pointing out that it is very difficult to solve a large number of problems in a short period of time, including the resumption of communications.
He called on the victims to be patient and said that the authorities would carry out reconstruction efforts as soon as possible.
On the other hand, Indonesia's Minister of Finance announced that the government has allocated 560 billion Indonesian guilders for disaster relief.
Guangdong Province Confirms a Case of H5N6 Avian Influenza
According to the latest notification from the mainland's health department, one person infected with H5N6 avian influenza has been confirmed in Guangdong Province.
The Health Bureau urged residents to avoid contact with birds and pay attention to personal and food hygiene.
According to the data, the patient is a 22-year-old man, now living in Baiyun District of Guangzhou, Guangdong Province; on September 25, he developed symptoms such as fever, was admitted to the hospital for treatment on September 26, and is currently isolated and treated in the hospital and in critical condition.
The patient was slaughtered and edible for live birds before the onset of the disease.
Since April 2014, there have been confirmed cases of H5N6 avian influenza in Sichuan, Guangdong, Yunnan, Hubei, Hunan, Anhui and Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region.
The Health Bureau will continue to maintain close contact with the health department of the country and neighboring regions, the World Health Organization, and closely monitor the epidemic situation in various places and in Macao.
In order to prevent human infection with avian influenza, the Health Bureau calls on the public to pay attention to the following matters:
Avoid contact with birds or their secretions and excretions; if there is contact, wash your hands immediately;
Do not buy or carry unquarantined birds;
Do not eat uncompromised poultry meat, internal organs, blood products and eggs;
Pay attention to personal hygiene and wash your hands frequently.
If there are symptoms such as fever, cough and breathing difficulties, you should wear a mask, seek medical treatment as soon as possible, and detail the travel history and animal contact history to the doctor.
