On the evening of the 29th, the reporter learned from the Propaganda Department of the Chengdu Qingbaijiang District Committee that on the evening of September 29, Beijing time, a China-Europe train (Chengdu) loaded with car connectors, telescopes, liquid crystal displays and other goods was changed through the Shemianufka port in Poland, and finally arrived in Nuremberg, Germany.
This is the first time that the domestic China-Europe train has opened the Shemianufka port line in Poland, which marks the successful opening of another European transportation line in China and Europe, after Mara and Chopp.
This China-Europe train started on September 14 by Chengdu Qingbaijiang City Station, exited through Alashankou, entered Europe through the Shemianufka port in Poland, and finally arrived in Nuremberg, Germany, for a total of about 16 days.
For the first time, the China-Europe train has carried out the replacement operation of the train's wide track and the marking track for the first time.
The opening of this port has effectively solved the problems caused by long-term operations and long-term problems caused by the current congestion at the Mara port, improved the aging of the train transportation; and provided a new solution to the congestion problem at the Mara port, further improved the carrying capacity and transportation efficiency of China's western hinterland to the European Mediterranean market, and laid a solid foundation for the development of the European market.
Indonesia's Sulawesi island, where a 7.5-magnitude quake struck on Friday, more than 400 people have been confirmed dead, many of whom have been swept away by the tsunami caused by the quake.
The authorities expect a significant increase in the total number of deaths on Sunday as new data is reported in remote areas.
Dozens of people are reportedly still trapped under the rubble of a hotel and a shopping mall in Baru.
Waves as high as six meters (20 feet), triggered by an earthquake, hit the city of Baru.
So far there is only the death toll from Baru, which has been reported slowly in Dungra in the north of Baru, where authorities are gearing up for something worse.
Dongra has a population of 300,000, closer to the epicenter of the earthquake.
Indonesia's vice president said the total number of deaths could rise to thousands.
When the twilight waves hit the coast on Friday, hundreds of people gathered on the beach to celebrate the festival, and many were swept away by the huge waves, and everything was destroyed wherever the waves went.
TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Confidence among Japan’s largest manufacturing players hit their lowest level in more than a year in September as rising raw material costs and a series of natural disasters affected production, according to the Bank of Japan’s quarterly survey on Monday.
Hardly this survey shows that the escalating global trade friction has hit the confidence of large manufacturers.
But the risk of an all-out trade war hitting business prospects could threaten corporate capital spending.
Active capital spending is a bright spot in Japan’s economy.
The survey calls into question the Bank of Japan’s view that a solid economic expansion will help drive inflation to an accelerated 2 percent target, although there are signs that companies are gradually passing on costs to their customers.
â€œIn the face of concerns caused by the global trade war, confidence among manufacturers is stagnating due to the slowdown in exports and weak factory production,â€ said Nan Wuzhi, chief researcher of the China National Institute of Agriculture and Forestry.
â€œConfidence is still high. And I don't think it's going to go down because corporate earnings are improving and prices are rising.â€
According to the short-term survey, in September, the index of large-scale manufacturing sentiment judgment dropped from positive 21 three months ago to 19, worsening for the third consecutive quarter.
The market’s median estimate is positive 22.
In September, the large non-manufacturing sentiment judgment index fell from positive 24 in the June survey to positive 22, the first deterioration in eight quarters.
The Reuters poll was 22.
According to the survey, the large-scale manufacturing and non-manufacturing performance indicators were expected to remain stable in December.
Investors are not concerned about the decline in the short-term corporate outlook, and the Nikkei .N225 rose to a 27-year high on Monday, as the yen’s continued depreciation has helped improve the export earnings prospects of Japanese companies.
Capital expenditures are stable.
Although business confidence has declined, the latest perspective highlights the soundness of corporate capital expenditure plans, thanks to the upgrading of production capacity and increased investment in robotics and automation to cope with labor shortages caused by an aging population.
According to the central bank's summary survey, large enterprises plan to increase capital expenditures by 13.4% in the current fiscal year ending in March 2019.
At the time of the previous survey, it was 13.6%.
Nan said that all corporate capital expenditure plans for this fiscal year will increase by 8.5%, which is close to the pace of Japan's bubble era.
â€œThere is still room for further growth in capital spending, given that small businesses have raised their profit forecasts from now on, but this largely depends on the impact of the trade war on business confidence,â€ he said.
The short-term survey shows an increase in the ability of companies to pass on costs, and the large enterprise output price index is positive 7, which is the highest point in a decade, which is an encouraging sign that Japan's efforts to combat deflation have made progress.
The index, which measures the employment status of large enterprises, hit negative 23, the tightest level since 1992 and highlighted the tightening labor market.
Thanks to strong corporate spending, Japan’s economy rebounded in the second quarter from its contraction in January-March.
However, the escalation of trade frictions in the summer and the disruption of the supply chain by natural disasters have clouded the economic prospects of Japan, which is dependent on exports.
In terms of U.S. dollars, the growth rate of service imports and exports was 16.4%.
According to the person in charge of the service and trade department, the total import and export of emerging services exceeded 1 trillion yuan in January-August, which was faster than the overall growth rate.
Among them, the total import and export of emerging services 113.839 billion yuan, an increase of 20.9%, higher than the overall growth rate of service imports and exports 10.4 percentage points, driving the proportion of emerging services increased by nearly 3 percentage points.
In terms of service exports, from January to August, service exports continued the rapid growth momentum since this year, and the growth rate of exports was 5.7 percentage points higher than that of imports.
Among them, the top three areas of growth are telecommunications computer and information services, personal culture and entertainment services, insurance services, the growth rate of 61.1%, 38.8% and 26.5%, respectively.
The person in charge of the Service Trade Division also pointed out that the proportion of emerging service imports in January-August has also gradually increased.
From January to August, the import of emerging services grew rapidly, accounting for 23.6% of service imports, an increase of 1.6 percentage points over the same period last year.
Among them, financial services, intellectual property royalties, telecommunications computer and information services import growth of more than 20%, respectively, 47.1%, 23.3% and 23.2%.
La Liga: Messi's substitute came to assist to draw the Barca League in three rounds.
La Liga 7th round of Barcelona home against Athletic Bilbao last night, De Marcos in the first half of the goal to help the away team lead, Messi second half came to assist Munir equalized, the two sides 1:1 draw ended, after this battle, Barcelona three rounds winless.
