Oil prices or ushered in the "three consecutive rises" National Day self-driving travel can be filled with oil in advance.
BEIJING, Sept. 30 (Reporter Qiu Yu) At 24:00 on September 30, a new round of refined oil price adjustment window will be synchronized with the National Day holiday.
Many institutions predict that oil prices will increase significantly, to achieve "three consecutive increases."
Owners who plan to travel by car can fill up the car before raising prices.
According to the data calculated by Longzhong information, it is expected that the corresponding increase in domestic refined oil products will be about 190 yuan / ton; the increase measured by Zhuochuang information is 220 yuan / ton.
In September, oil prices have been raised twice: on September 3, gasoline increased by 180 yuan / ton, diesel increased by 170 yuan / ton; on September 17, gasoline increased by 145 yuan / ton, diesel increased by 145 yuan / ton.
Domestic oil prices are pegged to international oil prices, and since the current round of pricing cycle, international oil prices have fluctuated, and Brent crude oil has continued to explore after breaking through the $80 mark.
As of the close on September 28, U.S. WTI crude oil futures closed up $1.13 at $73.25 per barrel.
Brent crude oil futures closed up $1.00 at $82.72 per barrel.
"Judging from the international situation, the United States imposed sanctions on Iran and other tensions, the overall trend of oil prices is stronger, and then the OPEC production reduction meeting clearly refused to increase production, giving market confidence, oil prices steadily moved up."
Zhuochuang information refined oil analyse analyst Yan Wengang said.
In terms of retail sales, the current gasoline prices of PetroChina and Sinopec gas stations in Beijing are 7.66 yuan / liter and 8.15 yuan / liter, respectively.
According to Longzhong information analyst Li Yan, the preferential promotion strategy of gas station retail has not changed much, and the current preferential range for main stations such as Sinopec is more than 0.5-0.7 yuan / liter, while the preferential range for private gas stations is more than 0.5-1.2 yuan / liter.
â€œThe current round of retail price is about to â€œthree consecutive riseâ€ , equivalent to an increase of about 0.14-0.16 yuan, it is recommended that private car owners fill up the oil before the arrival of the National Day holiday and travel again.
Primary school students do the wrong problem by the teacher's corporal punishment The school involved in the cancellation of the annual evaluation qualification-Zhongxin.com
In response to the incident of "Suining a small student who was wrongly punished by the teacher's corporal punishment" incident, the official Weibo of the Hedong New District Management Committee of Suining City issued an information notice yesterday, saying that after investigation, Luo XX, a teacher of Suizhou Foreign Language Primary School, had punished students for corporal punishment, had been transferred from the teacher's position, and the schools involved had cancelled their annual "evaluation" qualifications.
A few days ago, some parents reported that Suining a girl in the 6th grade of primary school was beaten by a class mathematics teacher in the school because she did the wrong problem, which caused widespread concern.
Subsequently, Suining Hedong New District Social Affairs Bureau set up an investigation team to enter the school to investigate the relevant personnel, enquire, collect evidence at the scene, and transfer the teachers involved away from the teacher's position.
Yesterday, the official micro-blog of Suining Hedong New District Management Committee issued a notice saying that after investigation, Luo XX, a teacher of Suizhou Foreign Language Primary School, punished students with corporal punishment.
After research, the Suizhou foreign language primary school year-end assessment "one veto", cancel the annual "evaluation" qualification.
According to the report, the administrative team of Suizhou Foreign Language Primary School will carry out a collective admonishment conversation, deal with the responsible leadership and class guidance in accordance with the relevant provisions of the relevant provisions; transfer Luo XX, the teacher involved, from the teacher's post, and deal with it seriously in accordance with the relevant provisions; order Suizhou Foreign Language Primary School to conduct in-depth inspections, and carry out the construction of teachers and teachers, and take practical measures to prevent the recurrence of such incidents.
At the same time, the school should take the initiative to communicate with the parents of the students and properly handle the follow-up work.
The 69th International Astronautical Congress Opens in Germany
Xinhua News Agency, Bremen, Germany, October 1 (Reporter Ren Ke Zhang Yirong) The 69th International Astronautical Congress kicked off on October 1 at the Bremen Exhibition Center in Germany, attended by more than 6,300 astronauts, representatives of space agencies and enterprises, experts, scholars and young students from all over the world.
In his opening address, IAF President Jean-Yves Lergar said that the global space industry is no longer attended by only a small number of countries and institutions, and this year's attendance has increased significantly compared with the previous session, indicating that more and more institutions and people are joining them.
He called on countries to strengthen cooperation and innovation and jointly promote the development of the space industry.
China's Vice Minister of Industry and Information Technology and Director-General of the National Space Administration, Zhang Kejun, introduced China's space program when attending the exchange event, and said that China will expand international cooperation in the space field and contribute to the human space industry.
China Aerospace Science and Technology Corporation, China Aerospace Science and Industry Corporation and other relevant institutions, as well as representatives of private enterprises attended the meeting, showing the latest achievements of China's aerospace industry, including various types of launch vehicles, satellites and space science and technology application products.
The International Astronautical Congress, held annually since 1950, is the world’s largest aviation event.
For five days, the conference was co-hosted by the International Astronautical Federation, the International Academy of Astronautics, the Center for Applied Technology and Microgravity Research at the University of Bremen and the International Society for Space Law.
BEIJING, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The Canton Fair shows that China's foreign trade situation is still complicated and severe, with 80.6 percent of companies expecting full-year exports in 2018 to be better than the previous year or flat, according to a press release issued by the China Foreign Trade Center on Sunday.
However, taking into account the continuous rise in the cost of domestic raw materials, labor and other comprehensive factors, and the external environment in which the impact of Sino-US trade frictions has increased, exhibitors also believe that next year's export situation is not optimistic.
At the closing press conference of the 124th Canton Fair, Xu Bing, deputy secretary-general of the Canton Fair, spokesman and deputy director of the China Foreign Trade Center, said that the number of overseas buyers and export transactions at this Canton Fair have decreased slightly year-on-year.
This year, 189,812 people from 215 countries and regions, down 1.11% year-on-year.
The export turnover of 2,06.494 billion yuan (equivalent to 29.86 billion US dollars), down 1% year-on-year.
From the perspective of the market, the turnover of Japan, the ten ASEAN countries, the "BRIC countries" and South Korea increased by 74.4%, 11.4%, 7.2% and 2.5% respectively, and the traditional markets of the United States, Australia, Canada and the European Union decreased by 30.3%, 8.9%, 7.3% and 0.8% respectively.
From the perspective of the industry, transportation tools, machinery and equipment, construction and decorative materials, consumer electronics and information products, and bathroom equipment increased by 24.8%, 21.1%, 20.01%, 15.1%, and 7.6% respectively, while textiles, clothing and household appliances decreased by 13.0% and 6.7% respectively.
Xu Bing said that as a barometer of China's foreign trade and the vane of the wind, the current Canton Trade Fair purchaser's situation and export transaction data show that China's foreign trade development is still facing many uncertain and unstable factors next year.
However, with the deepening of supply-side structural reform and the recent introduction of policy measures such as "six stability" by the national and local governments, the new momentum of China's foreign trade development is accelerating the accumulation, and the diversification of corporate markets continues to make new progress, which is an important basis and a strong condition for the development of foreign trade.
"Combined with various factors, it is expected that China's foreign trade imports and exports will maintain steady growth throughout the year, and the quality and efficiency will be further improved," Xu said.
China's General Administration of Customs announced that U.S. dollar-denominated exports increased by 14.5% year-on-year in September, imports increased by 14.3% year-on-year, the trade surplus in September was 31.69 billion U.S. dollars, and the export growth and trade surplus in September were the highest since February this year.
Despite the escalation of Sino-US trade frictions, China's export performance in September is still significantly higher than expected, strong external demand, enterprises in the United States before the imposition of tariffs on exports superimposed RMB exchange rate depreciation, or the main supporting factors, to some extent shows the resilience of China's foreign trade, but the Sino-US trade war on confidence, the impact on the industrial chain can not be underestimated, analysts believe that China's foreign trade challenges may appear in the fourth quarter or next year.
U.S. fund managers advised in September to increase their cash holdings and remain cautious as the U.S. and U.S. countries began the latest round of mutual import tariffs and no signs of détente.
However, according to the 12 fund managers participating in the survey, North America's asset allocation has increased to its highest level since June 2017, while positions in the United Kingdom, the euro area, especially in emerging markets, have declined.
Global stock allocation averaged 56.6 per cent, and bonds accounted for 35.5 per cent, which is basically the same as last month’s survey.
One of the most obvious changes is that the cash ratio has risen to 5.1%, the highest since December 2014.
"Some economic data brings confidence to the market, but the trade war is still the biggest concern, so it's best to be prepared to enter when the market falls back," said the fund manager of a large fund company.
However, fund managers still preferred stocks in September, especially U.S. stocks, even if U.S. stocks are considered to have high prices.
Today, Shanghai, China's open landmark, the world's first large-scale import-themed national-level exhibition, the China International Import Expo, officially kicked off in anticipation.
An exhibition is like a "window", allowing the world to better understand a city and a country.
Through the "window" of the Expo, people have seen the "opening of China" at a higher level; with the "window" of the Expo, they will welcome the mutually beneficial and win-win situation between the world and China's "reform and opening up".
"For a country, openness is like a cocoon into a butterfly, although it will experience a momentary pain, but it will be replaced by a new life."
General Secretary Xi Jinping's summary of the road of opening-up shows an important reason why China can do it.
Looking back on the 40 years of reform and opening up, China, which dares to enter the world's market, has encountered whirlpools and waves, it has always faced all risks and challenges with an open attitude, continuously released endogenous motivation, and continuously improved competitiveness.
It can be said that China's practical achievements have effectively interpreted the value and significance of opening up.
Standing at a new historical starting point and holding an import-themed exposition is a major decision made by the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping as the core to promote a new round of high-level opening-up, which is China's major initiative to open its market to the world, China's practical actions to support economic globalization and trade liberalization, showing that "China's open door will not be closed, but will only open more and wider".
Exhibitors from all over the world are actively registered, and the booth "one is difficult to find" is the biggest affirmation and the best response to China's development of an open economy on a larger scale, in a wider range, in a wider field, and at a deeper level.
More importantly, the current global economic and trade order has reached a crossroads.
Some countries have built a high wall of trade protectionism and returned to the old path of unilateralism, increasing the international community's concerns about the prospects for free trade and adding many uncertainties to the rising world economy.
In the context of such an era, this event on the banks of the Huangpu River reflects China's defense of free trade, allowing the world to see China's self-confidence in opening up the market and sharing the future and China's responsibility.
Go alone, go far away.
China's openness and embrace of the world not only effectively promoted its own development, but also brought surging "Chinese opportunities" to countries and regions around the world.
In recent years, advocating and promoting the joint construction of the "Belt and Road", launching the establishment of the AIIB, and setting up the Silk Road Fund... China has provided a series of international public goods, providing real export markets, development opportunities and jobs, so that enterprises of all countries can take the "fast train" and "free ride" of China's development.
The Expo is also a public product and a big platform for global economic and trade cooperation.
On top of this platform, more than 3,000 enterprises from more than 130 countries and regions have taken a new step in the Chinese market with their own high-quality products and services.
In addition to national enterprises, there are domestic consumers who really benefit.
By building this "optimal and preferred" platform, we will provide high-quality supply of multiple channels for consumption upgrading, and meet the personalized, diversified and differentiated consumption needs of the people.
As China's open door is opening wider and wider, the goods will flow smoothly and make the most of them, and the pace of moving towards a better life will be more solid.
From a broader perspective, the significance of the Expo has gone beyond the scope of economy and trade, but focuses on the future, conveys the concept of openness, inclusiveness, inclusiveness, balance and win-win, and forms a consensus to jointly address today's challenges.
If the world is good, China can be good; if China is good, the world is better.
We look forward to the Expo to bring greatness and success to the world; we look forward to moving to a higher level of "open China" with the world to build a glorious future of a community with a shared future for mankind.
Foreign media: the United States and Canada reached a framework agreement on the North American Free Trade Agreement.
The agreement includes Canada’s opening of its dairy market to the United States, as well as temporary U.S. tariffs on Canadian-made cars.
According to foreign media reports, a Canadian source revealed on the evening of September 30 that the United States and Canada have reached a framework agreement on the North American Free Trade Agreement.
According to reports, the agreement includes Canada's opening of its dairy market to the United States, as well as the temporary imposition of tariffs by the United States on Canadian-made cars.
On July 27, the United States and Mexico announced that they had reached a preliminary agreement in principle on updating the North American Free Trade Agreement, but the United States and Canada failed to reach an agreement before the August 31 deadline set by the United States to extend the negotiation period until September 30.
Earlier, a spokesman for Canada's foreign minister, Freeland, said that Canada would only sign a favorable agreement, "focusing on the substance, not the timetable. We will continue to consult, hoping to reach an agreement that is in Canada's national interest."
More than 90 percent of Brazil’s female voters said the presidential candidates did not take women’s needs into account.
According to data released by Brazil's National Geographic Research Institute (IBGE), more than 90% of Brazilian women do not believe that presidential candidates take women's needs into account.
According to the report, the number of women in Brazil has reached 107 million people, and if the women of all Brazil are gathered to form a country, then the country's population will rank 13th in the world, more than twice the population of Spain.
In Brazil, women account for 52% of all voters and 48% of men. Although the proportion of women among voters is very high, only 10% are women in Brazil's Congress.
Among the 193 countries in the world, Brazilian women are only ranked 154th in terms of political participation, which is higher than that of Arab countries.
After more than two decades of struggle for rights, Brazilian women have still not succeeded in obtaining the rights they deserve.
According to Brazilian sociologist Natalia Mori, this phenomenon exists as a result of the combination of ancient patrilineal societies, racism, and capitalist values.
“Politics should have been made up of citizens for civil rights, identity, access to public goods, and the formation of the same society by multiple social groups. But Brazilian politics belongs to the monopoly of one group, and the majority of the population is not represented.”
According to a previous study conducted by Locomotiva, 94% of Brazilian women do not feel that elected politicians can represent their rights, 90% of Brazilian women do not agree with the decisions made by politicians, and 93% do not agree with the current government policy.
â€œWe need to reverse the underrepresentation of women in parliament. Brazil's political system is still affected by inequality. So far, there are still serious genders, classes, and racial discrimination in Brazil's political sphere,â€ said Natalia Mori.
Despite women’s rights, the majority of Brazilian women still believe in the power of democracy.
According to the survey, 76% of women believe that they can make a difference in democratic elections, and 72% are interested in politics.
In addition, 55% of women believe that democratic politics is the best way to expose women to less prejudice.
Astana, October 1 (Reporter Wen Longjie) The Chinese Embassy in Kazakhstan held a solemn flag-raising ceremony on October 1 to welcome the 69-year-old birthday of New China.
More than 80 representatives of the Chinese Embassy in Kazakhstan, news agencies, financial institutions, Chinese-funded enterprises, overseas Chinese, Confucius Institutes and international students participated in the event.
On October 1st, the Chinese Embassy in Kazakhstan held a flag-raising ceremony to celebrate the 69th birthday of New China.
After the flag-raising ceremony, China's Ambassador to Kazakhstan Zhang Xiao said that on the occasion of the 69th birthday of the great motherland, we solemnly held a flag-raising ceremony in foreign countries, which is a profound patriotic education event.
Although we have been living overseas for a long time, we are always concerned about the great motherland.
Zhang Xiao said that the Chinese nation today is closer than ever to achieving the great goal of national rejuvenation and closer to the center of the world stage than ever before.
â€œOur mission, responsibilities, and work are more honorable, arduous, and onerous than ever before.â€
Zhang Xiao stressed that it is necessary not to forget the original intention, keep in mind the mission, promote the China-Kazakhstan joint construction of the "Belt and Road" steady and far-reaching, deep and practical, draw a more beautiful co-construction of the "Belt and Road" and "work strokes", and dedicate all forces to the development and construction of the motherland and the friendly cooperation between China and Kazakhstan.
Guangxi Guilin Liangjiang International Airport T2 terminal was officially opened on the 30th.
Zhao Leqin, secretary of the Guilin Municipal Party Committee of the Communist Party of China, said that after the opening of the new terminal, it can meet the needs of 12 million passengers per year, and built a new advantage of Guilin air transportation, which is of great significance to further improve the modern three-dimensional traffic pattern of Guangxi Jianghai linkage, sea and rail intermodal transportation, water and land development, and air and port connection.
This year, Guilin is expected to receive more than 90 million tourists.
Guilin Liangjiang International Airport T2 terminal and platform supporting facilities expansion project, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region 60th anniversary of Daqing's major public welfare projects, but also Guilin international tourist destination construction of the landmark project.
The project started construction in December 2015, with a construction area of 100,000 square meters and a total investment of 3.258 billion yuan, which can meet the annual passenger throughput of 12 million passengers, 10,1200 take-offs and landings, and 95,000 tons of cargo and mail throughput.
On the same day, more than 200 flights took off and landed at Terminal T2 of Guilin Liangjiang International Airport.
The design of the new terminal is inspired by Guilin's mountains and waters, and looks like a "mountain laurel crown", similar to the "Long ridge terraces" and the cascaded eaves of Guibei's dwellings.
According to reports, Guilin Airport's new terminal can meet the peak traffic of nearly 4,000 people per hour in and out of Hong Kong, the application of intelligent luggage sorting system, security integration platform, face recognition and other "intelligent airport" technical means, planning covers catering, department stores, duty-free and entertainment and other forms of business areas.
